window.DOCS_DATA = {"structure": {"intro": "This repository is a Python simulation package (<code>sandbox</code>) built <strong>bottom-up in strict dependency tiers</strong> — Tier 0 modules depend on nothing else in the package, Tier 1 depends only on Tier 0, Tier 2 depends only on Tier 0/1, and so on. As of this documentation, <strong>Tier 0, Tier 1, and Tier 2 are fully implemented and unit-tested</strong>; the integration tier (a <code>simulation_orchestrator.py</code> that wires every other module into the per-turn simulation loop, plus an undesigned <code>prompt_builder.py</code>) is <strong>planned but not yet written</strong> — see the Architecture tab for what that means concretely. Two long-form Markdown documents under <code>Architecture-docs/</code> are the authoritative design spec that every built module is a direct port of; <code>plan.md</code> and <code>phase3.md</code> are the incremental build logs that record the specific design decisions made while turning that spec into code.", "tree": "Agentic networks/\n├── sandbox/                     # The Python package: all simulation logic\n│   ├── __init__.py               # Empty package marker\n│   ├── models.py                 # Tier 0 — Pydantic schemas shared by every module\n│   ├── config_loader.py          # Tier 0 — YAML run-config parsing & validation\n│   ├── seed_manager.py           # Tier 0 — seeded RNG streams for reproducibility\n│   ├── cost_tracker.py           # Tier 0 — per-call $ cost accounting + ceiling\n│   ├── rate_limiter.py           # Tier 0 — per-provider request throttling\n│   ├── agent_manager.py          # Tier 1 — creates/holds/mutates the Agent population\n│   ├── meme_pool_manager.py      # Tier 1 — loads meme dataset, decides injections\n│   ├── model_gateway.py          # Tier 1 — normalized async LLM call interface (LiteLLM)\n│   ├── interaction_engine.py     # Tier 2 — alpha-weighted neighbor selection\n│   ├── stance_parser.py          # Tier 2 — extracts stance value + reason from model text\n│   ├── vision_fallback.py        # Tier 2 — caption-only prompt substitution\n│   ├── logging_writer.py         # Tier 2 — append-only JSONL persistence\n│   └── checkpoint_manager.py     # Tier 2 — per-turn checkpoint save/resume\n│\n├── tests/                        # pytest suite, one file per sandbox/ module\n│   ├── conftest.py                # shared fixtures (valid_config_dict, write_config)\n│   └── test_*.py                  # one test module per sandbox/ module (13 files)\n│\n├── data/                         # Input assets read by the simulation at run time\n│   ├── personas/\n│   │   ├── test_pool.jsonl         # 4-persona fixture used across most tests\n│   │   └── pool_20.jsonl           # 20-persona fixture, exercises pool-cycling\n│   └── memes/\n│       ├── test_pool.jsonl         # 3-item MemeContent fixture\n│       ├── empty_pool.jsonl        # zero-line fixture for the empty-pool error path\n│       └── images/\n│           └── test_001.jpg         # tiny real JPEG so vision_fallback's success path works\n│\n├── runs/                         # Output directory — one subdirectory per simulation run\n│   └── .gitkeep                   # currently empty; populated by logging_writer.py at run time\n│\n├── Architecture-docs/            # Stable, long-form design specification\n│   ├── sandbox_hld.md             # High-level design + 3 passes of adversarial self-critique\n│   └── full_design_doc.md         # Low-level design: per-module LLD, schemas, storage, API\n│\n├── plan.md                       # Phase 2 build log (Tier 1: agent/meme/gateway) — merged\n├── phase3.md                     # Phase 3 build log (Tier 2 modules) — merged\n├── pricing_table.yaml            # Hand-maintained $-per-1k-token pricing, by provider/model/modality\n├── pyproject.toml                # Package metadata, dependencies, pytest config\n├── README.md                     # One-line pointer to the architecture diagram image\n├── agentic-network.png           # Architecture diagram referenced by README.md\n└── CLAUDE.md                     # Instructions for AI coding agents working in this repo\n", "legend": [{"label": "Tier 0 — pure data & standalone infra", "color": "tier0"}, {"label": "Tier 1 — depends only on Tier 0", "color": "tier1"}, {"label": "Tier 2 — depends only on Tier 0/1", "color": "tier2"}, {"label": "Tier 3 — integration (planned, not built)", "color": "tier3"}, {"label": "Config / data file", "color": "config"}, {"label": "Test module", "color": "accent"}], "folders": [{"path": "sandbox/", "description": "The installable Python package (<code>pyproject.toml</code> declares it as <code>name = \"sandbox\"</code>, importable as <code>import sandbox</code>). Every runtime module lives directly under this one flat directory — there are no sub-packages. The build order and allowed-dependency direction between these 13 files is the single most important organizing fact about this codebase; see the Architecture tab for the full dependency graph."}, {"path": "tests/", "description": "A 1:1 pytest module per <code>sandbox/</code> module (<code>test_agent_manager.py</code> tests <code>agent_manager.py</code>, etc.), plus <code>conftest.py</code> for fixtures shared mainly by the config-loader and logging-writer tests. <code>pyproject.toml</code> sets <code>asyncio_mode = \"auto\"</code>, so <code>async def test_*</code> functions (used for the model gateway and logging writer's concurrency tests) run without needing <code>@pytest.mark.asyncio</code> decorators."}, {"path": "data/personas/", "description": "Plain-text persona pools — one free-text persona description per line, <strong>not</strong> JSON-wrapped (a deliberate simplification: a persona is just a string in this scope). <code>agent_manager.py</code> cycles through a pool's lines when <code>M</code> (population size) exceeds the pool's length."}, {"path": "data/memes/", "description": "One JSONL file per meme pool, each line a <code>MemeContent</code> record (<code>meme_id</code>, <code>image_path</code>, <code>caption_text</code>, <code>stance_label</code>, <code>offensiveness_label</code>, <code>source_dataset</code>). <code>empty_pool.jsonl</code> exists purely to exercise <code>meme_pool_manager.py</code>'s empty-pool <code>ValueError</code> path. <code>images/</code> holds the actual JPEG bytes that <code>image_path</code> fields point at — only <code>test_001.jpg</code> currently exists on disk (the other two paths referenced in <code>test_pool.jsonl</code> do not resolve to real files, which is fine since no test currently loads them)."}, {"path": "runs/", "description": "Output directory for completed/in-progress simulation runs, per <code>logging_writer.py</code> and <code>checkpoint_manager.py</code>'s design: one subdirectory per <code>run_id</code>, containing <code>run_config.json</code>, <code>interactions.jsonl</code>, <code>agents_final.jsonl</code>, and a <code>checkpoints/</code> subdirectory. Currently empty (only a <code>.gitkeep</code>) because no orchestrator exists yet to actually launch a run."}, {"path": "Architecture-docs/", "description": "The stable specification. <code>sandbox_hld.md</code> is the system-level design plus three rounds of self-critique (its own \"Fix A\" through \"Fix N\" numbered resolutions); <code>full_design_doc.md</code> goes one level deeper — concrete function signatures, error-handling contracts, and concurrency notes for every module, plus the full Pydantic schema and on-disk storage layout. Every built <code>sandbox/*.py</code> module's own docstring cites which section of which document it is a \"direct port\" of."}, {"path": "top level (plan.md, phase3.md, pricing_table.yaml, pyproject.toml)", "description": "<code>plan.md</code> and <code>phase3.md</code> are per-phase build logs — each one plans a tier before it's implemented, resolves any design gaps the architecture docs left open (e.g. exactly how <code>memory_window</code> is maintained), and lists the acceptance-criteria tests to write. <code>pricing_table.yaml</code> is the hand-maintained $/1k-token table <code>cost_tracker.py</code> reads. <code>pyproject.toml</code> declares the package, its runtime/dev dependencies, and pytest configuration."}]}, "files": {"sandbox/__init__.py": {"path": "sandbox/__init__.py", "tier": "tier0", "oneLiner": "Empty package marker — makes sandbox/ importable as a package.", "overview": ["This file is completely empty. Its only purpose is to mark the <code>sandbox/</code> directory as a regular Python package so that <code>import sandbox.models</code>, <code>import sandbox.agent_manager</code>, etc. work.", "It exports nothing and re-exports nothing — every consumer (including the test suite) imports directly from the specific submodule it needs, e.g. <code>from sandbox.models import Agent</code>."], "dependencies": []}, "sandbox/models.py": {"path": "sandbox/models.py", "tier": "tier0", "oneLiner": "The Pydantic v2 schema shared by every other module — Agent, Interaction, MemeContent, ExperimentRun, etc.", "overview": ["Defines every structured data type the sandbox passes between modules and persists to disk, as <strong>Pydantic v2 <code>BaseModel</code> subclasses</strong> (not dataclasses — the design docs' own dataclass sketches are explicitly superseded by these Pydantic models, per this file's own docstring).", "It exists to give every other module a single, validated vocabulary: an <code>Agent</code> means the same thing to <code>agent_manager.py</code>, <code>interaction_engine.py</code>, and <code>logging_writer.py</code> alike, and invalid data (an out-of-range stance, a malformed language condition, N ≥ M) is rejected at construction time rather than discovered downstream.", "This is the one module every other <code>sandbox/*.py</code> file depends on, directly or indirectly — it sits at the base of the dependency tier system with no dependencies of its own beyond <code>pydantic</code>."], "dependencies": [], "dependents": ["sandbox/config_loader.py", "sandbox/agent_manager.py", "sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py", "sandbox/model_gateway.py", "sandbox/interaction_engine.py", "sandbox/vision_fallback.py", "sandbox/logging_writer.py", "sandbox/checkpoint_manager.py", "sandbox/cost_tracker.py"], "classes": [{"name": "StanceRecord", "purpose": "One historical stance update, embedded as a list inside <code>Agent.stance_history</code> (one entry appended per turn the agent successfully speaks).", "attributes": [{"name": "turn", "type": "int (≥1)", "desc": "Which simulation turn this record was produced on."}, {"name": "stance_value", "type": "float", "desc": "The agent's stance immediately after this turn."}, {"name": "reason_text", "type": "str", "desc": "The free-text justification produced for this stance update (the parsed model output, or empty for some failure/meme cases)."}, {"name": "interaction_id", "type": "str", "desc": "Links back to the Interaction record this stance update came from."}]}, {"name": "Agent", "purpose": "One simulated participant. Holds identity (<code>agent_id</code>, <code>persona</code>), configuration copied from the run (<code>language_condition</code>, <code>model_backend_id</code>), and mutable state (<code>stance_history</code>, <code>memory_window</code>).", "attributes": [{"name": "agent_id", "type": "str", "desc": "e.g. \"agent_0042\" — unique within a run."}, {"name": "run_id", "type": "str", "desc": "Foreign key to the owning ExperimentRun."}, {"name": "persona", "type": "str (min length 1)", "desc": "Free-text persona description used in prompt construction."}, {"name": "language_condition", "type": "str, one of english|hinglish|hindi", "desc": "Regex-constrained via Field(pattern=...)."}, {"name": "model_backend_id", "type": "str", "desc": "e.g. \"gpt-4o\" — single backend per run, identical for every agent in that run."}, {"name": "initial_stance", "type": "float", "desc": "The agent's stance before turn 1, drawn uniformly from the run's stance_scale."}, {"name": "stance_history", "type": "list[StanceRecord]", "desc": "Append-only; empty until the agent's first successful turn."}, {"name": "memory_window", "type": "list[str], max 5 entries", "desc": "Schema-capped pointer to this agent's own most recent up-to-5 interaction_ids (see agent_manager.py's apply_interaction() for how this is maintained)."}, {"name": "created_at_turn", "type": "int", "desc": "Always 0 in the current design (no mid-run agent creation)."}], "methods": [{"name": "current_stance", "signature": "def current_stance(self) -> float:", "behavior": "Returns the <code>stance_value</code> of the last entry in <code>stance_history</code> if it is non-empty, otherwise returns <code>initial_stance</code>. This is a convenience for code that has an <code>Agent</code> object in hand (e.g. post-hoc analysis loading <code>agents_final.jsonl</code>) — note that <code>interaction_engine.py</code>'s own internal <code>_current_stance()</code> deliberately duplicates this exact logic rather than calling this method (a documented fidelity-to-spec choice, not an oversight).", "input": [], "output": {"type": "float", "desc": "The agent's current stance."}}]}, {"name": "MemeContent", "purpose": "One entry in a meme dataset (loaded from a <code>data/memes/*.jsonl</code> pool file). Represents pre-existing, pre-labeled meme content that can replace an agent's generated post.", "attributes": [{"name": "meme_id", "type": "str", "desc": "Unique id within its pool."}, {"name": "image_path", "type": "str", "desc": "Filesystem path to the meme image, read lazily by vision_fallback.py — not validated to exist at load time."}, {"name": "caption_text", "type": "str (min length 1)", "desc": "Enforced non-empty at the schema level, since a caption-less meme could never be shown to a text-only-backend receiver."}, {"name": "stance_label", "type": "float", "desc": "Pre-existing dataset label, used directly as this meme's stance for neighbor-sampling purposes."}, {"name": "offensiveness_label", "type": "float | None", "desc": "Optional pre-existing dataset label."}, {"name": "source_dataset", "type": "str", "desc": "Provenance string, e.g. dataset name/version."}]}, {"name": "Interaction", "purpose": "The core, load-bearing record of the whole system — one row per agent-turn, written to <code>interactions.jsonl</code>. Every downstream metric (Ohagi-style regression, bimodality, coherence scoring) is computed from a DataFrame built out of these rows.", "attributes": [{"name": "interaction_id", "type": "str", "desc": "uuid4."}, {"name": "run_id", "type": "str", "desc": "Foreign key to the ExperimentRun."}, {"name": "turn", "type": "int (≥1)", "desc": ""}, {"name": "speaker_agent_id", "type": "str", "desc": "Foreign key to Agent.agent_id."}, {"name": "neighbor_agent_ids", "type": "list[str] (min length 1)", "desc": "The N agents sampled this turn whose posts the speaker saw."}, {"name": "stance_before", "type": "float", "desc": "The speaker's stance at the start of this turn."}, {"name": "stance_after", "type": "float", "desc": "The speaker's stance after this turn (the meme's stance_label, for meme turns)."}, {"name": "reason_text", "type": "str", "desc": "Free-text justification, or empty/caption text depending on content_type and failure state."}, {"name": "content_type", "type": "str, generated_text|meme", "desc": ""}, {"name": "meme_id", "type": "str | None", "desc": "Non-null iff content_type == \"meme\" — enforced by a cross-field model_validator."}, {"name": "used_vision_fallback", "type": "bool", "desc": "True if a text-only receiver got the meme's caption-only fallback instead of image+caption."}, {"name": "prompt_token_count", "type": "int (≥0)", "desc": "0 for meme-posting turns (no LLM call is made)."}, {"name": "completion_token_count", "type": "int (≥0)", "desc": ""}, {"name": "model_backend_id", "type": "str", "desc": ""}, {"name": "latency_ms", "type": "int (≥0)", "desc": ""}, {"name": "api_call_status", "type": "str, success|retried_success|failed_logged_null", "desc": ""}, {"name": "timestamp_utc", "type": "str (ISO 8601)", "desc": ""}], "methods": [{"name": "check_meme_id_consistency", "signature": "@model_validator(mode=\"after\")\ndef check_meme_id_consistency(self) -> \"Interaction\":", "behavior": "Cross-field validation: raises <code>ValueError</code> if <code>content_type == \"meme\"</code> but <code>meme_id</code> is <code>None</code>, or if <code>content_type == \"generated_text\"</code> but <code>meme_id</code> is not <code>None</code>. Runs automatically on every <code>Interaction</code> construction; not called directly by other modules.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "Interaction", "desc": "self, unchanged, if valid."}}, {"name": "is_valid_for_analysis", "signature": "@property\ndef is_valid_for_analysis(self) -> bool:", "behavior": "Convenience property for post-hoc analysis code to filter out soft-failed rows before computing metrics.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "bool", "desc": "True unless api_call_status == \"failed_logged_null\"."}}]}, {"name": "MemeInjectionConfig", "purpose": "Embedded config block on ExperimentRun controlling whether and how memes replace generated posts.", "attributes": [{"name": "enabled", "type": "bool, default False", "desc": ""}, {"name": "meme_pool_id", "type": "str | None", "desc": "Required (non-null) when enabled=True."}, {"name": "injection_rate", "type": "float in [0,1], default 0.0", "desc": "Per-agent-turn probability of a meme injection under the \"random\" schedule."}, {"name": "injection_schedule", "type": "str, random|fixed_turn, default \"random\"", "desc": ""}, {"name": "fixed_turns", "type": "set[int]", "desc": "Required non-empty when injection_schedule == \"fixed_turn\"."}], "methods": [{"name": "check_enabled_requirements", "signature": "@model_validator(mode=\"after\")\ndef check_enabled_requirements(self) -> \"MemeInjectionConfig\":", "behavior": "If <code>enabled</code> is True: raises <code>ValueError</code> if <code>meme_pool_id</code> is <code>None</code>; raises <code>ValueError</code> if <code>injection_schedule == \"fixed_turn\"</code> and <code>fixed_turns</code> is empty.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "MemeInjectionConfig", "desc": "self, unchanged, if valid."}}]}, {"name": "ExperimentRun", "purpose": "The top-level config/metadata object for one simulation execution — what <code>config_loader.load_run_config()</code> produces, and what every other constructor in the system (AgentManager, CostTracker, MemePoolManager, …) takes as its primary input.", "attributes": [{"name": "run_id", "type": "str", "desc": "Also the runs/ output directory name."}, {"name": "rq_target", "type": "str, RQ1_RQ2|RQ3|RQ1_RQ2_RQ3", "desc": ""}, {"name": "mode", "type": "str, fixed to \"multi_turn\"", "desc": "Single allowed value; retained as a field for forward-compatibility only."}, {"name": "topic", "type": "str (min length 1)", "desc": ""}, {"name": "alpha", "type": "float in [0,1]", "desc": "Homophily strength for neighbor sampling."}, {"name": "M", "type": "int (≥2)", "desc": "Population size."}, {"name": "N", "type": "int (≥1), and N < M (cross-field validator)", "desc": "Neighbors sampled per agent per turn."}, {"name": "K", "type": "int (≥1)", "desc": "Number of turns."}, {"name": "trial_number", "type": "int (≥1)", "desc": ""}, {"name": "language_condition", "type": "str, english|hinglish|hindi", "desc": ""}, {"name": "model_backend_id", "type": "str (min length 1)", "desc": "Single backend for the whole run — no cross-model sweep."}, {"name": "stance_scale", "type": "list[float] (min length 2)", "desc": "The finite scale agents' stances are drawn from and validated against."}, {"name": "persona_pool_id", "type": "str (min length 1)", "desc": ""}, {"name": "meme_injection", "type": "MemeInjectionConfig", "desc": "Defaults to a disabled config."}, {"name": "seed", "type": "int", "desc": "Feeds SeedManager; not an LLM sampling seed."}, {"name": "temperature", "type": "float in [0,2]", "desc": ""}, {"name": "max_cost_usd", "type": "float | None, > 0.0 if set", "desc": ""}, {"name": "rate_limits", "type": "dict[str,int]", "desc": "Provider name -> requests/minute."}, {"name": "checkpoint_every_n_turns", "type": "int (≥1), default 1", "desc": ""}, {"name": "git_commit_hash", "type": "str, default \"\"", "desc": "Populated by config_loader.py at load time; never user-supplied."}, {"name": "started_at_utc", "type": "str | None", "desc": ""}, {"name": "completed_at_utc", "type": "str | None", "desc": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": "str, default \"pending\"", "desc": "pending|running|completed|failed_partial|failed_total"}, {"name": "total_cost_usd", "type": "float, default 0.0", "desc": ""}], "methods": [{"name": "check_n_less_than_m", "signature": "@model_validator(mode=\"after\")\ndef check_n_less_than_m(self) -> \"ExperimentRun\":", "behavior": "Raises ValueError if N >= M — you cannot sample N distinct non-self neighbors from a population of M if N is not strictly smaller than M.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "ExperimentRun", "desc": "self, unchanged, if valid."}}]}, {"name": "CheckpointState", "purpose": "What checkpoint_manager.py serializes to/from runs/{run_id}/checkpoints/latest.json.", "attributes": [{"name": "run_id", "type": "str", "desc": ""}, {"name": "last_completed_turn", "type": "int", "desc": ""}, {"name": "agent_snapshot", "type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "Full serialized state of every agent as of the end of last_completed_turn."}]}]}, "sandbox/config_loader.py": {"path": "sandbox/config_loader.py", "tier": "tier0", "oneLiner": "Parses a YAML run config into a validated ExperimentRun, failing loudly before any budget is spent.", "overview": ["Reads a YAML file, validates it against the <code>ExperimentRun</code> Pydantic schema, resolves the current git commit hash, and confirms that any referenced persona/meme pool files actually exist on disk — all before returning.", "It exists as the mandatory first gate of every run: nothing else in the system is permitted to act until a config has cleared this function, so that a bad config (invalid alpha, a missing persona pool, N ≥ M) is caught immediately rather than after API calls have already been made.", "It is the sole producer of <code>ExperimentRun</code> objects from user-authored YAML; every other Tier 0/1/2 constructor that takes an <code>ExperimentRun</code> (AgentManager, CostTracker, MemePoolManager's config, …) ultimately receives the object this module built.", "Depends only on <code>sandbox/models.py</code> (for <code>ExperimentRun</code>) plus the stdlib, <code>pyyaml</code>, and <code>pydantic</code>."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/models.py"], "classes": [{"name": "ConfigLoadError", "purpose": "The single exception type this module raises for any config problem — file-not-found, malformed YAML, empty file, schema-validation failure, or a missing referenced asset.", "attributes": [{"name": "path", "type": "Path", "desc": "The config file path that failed to load."}, {"name": "errors", "type": "list[str]", "desc": "Every problem found, not just the first — see load_run_config()'s accumulation behavior."}], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, path: Path, errors: list[str]):", "input": [{"name": "path", "type": "Path", "desc": "The config file path."}, {"name": "errors", "type": "list[str]", "desc": "Human-readable error strings, joined into the exception message."}]}}], "functions": [{"name": "load_run_config", "signature": "def load_run_config(path: Path) -> ExperimentRun:", "behavior": "1) Raises <code>ConfigLoadError</code> if the file doesn't exist. 2) Parses YAML via <code>yaml.safe_load</code>, wrapping <code>yaml.YAMLError</code> and an empty/<code>None</code> parse result into <code>ConfigLoadError</code>. 3) Strips any user-supplied <code>git_commit_hash</code> key and replaces it with the real current commit hash from <code>git rev-parse HEAD</code> (via <code>_resolve_git_commit_hash</code>) — a repo with no commits or that isn't a git repo is treated as a fatal config-load failure. 4) Attempts to construct <code>ExperimentRun(**raw)</code>; Pydantic <code>ValidationError</code>s are collected as strings rather than raised immediately. 5) <strong>Independently of whether step 4 succeeded</strong>, checks that any referenced <code>persona_pool_id</code> / (if <code>meme_injection.enabled</code>) <code>meme_pool_id</code> resolve to real files under <code>data/personas/</code> / <code>data/memes/</code>, appending any missing-asset errors to the same list. 6) If the combined error list is non-empty, raises one <code>ConfigLoadError</code> listing everything found; otherwise returns the validated <code>ExperimentRun</code>.", "input": [{"name": "path", "type": "Path", "desc": "Filesystem path to a YAML run config."}], "output": {"type": "ExperimentRun", "desc": "A fully validated run config. Never a partially valid object."}, "notes": "<strong>Deliberately deviates from the sample code in <code>full_design_doc.md</code> §3.1</strong>, which raises immediately on the first Pydantic error and never reaches the filesystem check. That sample code cannot satisfy the feature's own acceptance criterion (\"a config with two independent errors — e.g. bad alpha and missing persona pool — produces ONE ConfigLoadError listing both\"), so this implementation follows the higher-authority acceptance criterion instead of the doc's literal sample code."}, {"name": "_resolve_git_commit_hash", "signature": "def _resolve_git_commit_hash() -> str:", "behavior": "Runs <code>git rev-parse HEAD</code> via <code>subprocess.run</code>. If the working directory isn't a git repo, or has zero commits (or <code>git</code> isn't installed), catches <code>CalledProcessError</code>/<code>FileNotFoundError</code> and re-raises as <code>ConfigLoadError</code> — never falls back to an empty string, since that would make <code>git_commit_hash</code> useless for tracing which code version produced a run.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "str", "desc": "The full 40-character SHA of the current HEAD commit."}}, {"name": "_referenced_asset_errors", "signature": "def _referenced_asset_errors(raw: dict) -> list[str]:", "behavior": "Reads directly from the raw dict (not a validated <code>ExperimentRun</code>), so this check runs regardless of whether schema validation itself succeeded. If <code>meme_injection.enabled</code> is True, checks <code>data/memes/{meme_pool_id}.jsonl</code> exists. Always checks <code>data/personas/{persona_pool_id}.jsonl</code> exists. Appends a descriptive error string (naming the missing path) for each failure found.", "input": [{"name": "raw", "type": "dict", "desc": "The raw, possibly Pydantic-invalid, parsed YAML dict."}], "output": {"type": "list[str]", "desc": "All missing-asset error strings found (zero, one, or two)."}}]}, "sandbox/seed_manager.py": {"path": "sandbox/seed_manager.py", "tier": "tier0", "oneLiner": "Hands out three independently-seeded random.Random streams (neighbor sampling, meme injection, persona assignment) from one base seed.", "overview": ["Provides three separate, purpose-specific <code>random.Random</code> instances, deterministically offset (<code>seed</code>, <code>seed+1</code>, <code>seed+2</code>) from a single top-level seed, so the three streams never accidentally correlate.", "It exists so every non-LLM stochastic decision in the system (which neighbors get sampled, whether a turn is a meme injection, which persona/initial-stance an agent gets) is fully reproducible given the same seed — and so that reusing the same top-level seed across two different <code>ExperimentRun</code> configs (e.g. an English-condition run and a Hinglish-condition run in the same sweep) reproduces identical meme-injection and neighbor-sampling draw sequences across both, isolating the language variable from those confounds.", "It makes <strong>no claim about LLM sampling determinism</strong> — provider APIs do not guarantee deterministic output even at temperature=0, so the seed only controls this system's own non-LLM randomness.", "Consumed by whatever constructs <code>AgentManager</code> (persona_assignment_rng), <code>MemePoolManager</code> (meme_injection_rng), and <code>AlphaSampling.select_neighbors()</code> callers (neighbor_sampling_rng) — in the current codebase, that wiring happens in each module's own tests; the not-yet-built Orchestrator will be the real production caller."], "dependencies": [], "classes": [{"name": "SeedManager", "purpose": "One instance per run. Each property returns the <strong>same long-lived <code>random.Random</code> instance</strong> on every access — not a fresh one — since each stream advances as consuming features draw from it.", "attributes": [{"name": "neighbor_sampling_rng", "type": "random.Random (property)", "desc": "Seeded with the base seed, unmodified."}, {"name": "meme_injection_rng", "type": "random.Random (property)", "desc": "Seeded with base seed + 1."}, {"name": "persona_assignment_rng", "type": "random.Random (property)", "desc": "Seeded with base seed + 2."}], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, seed: int):", "input": [{"name": "seed", "type": "int", "desc": "The run's top-level seed."}]}}], "notes": ["Assumes neighbor-sampling and meme-injection resolution happen strictly sequentially within a turn, never concurrently with each other — so these <code>random.Random</code> instances are never accessed concurrently and need no internal locking. If a future change ever parallelized those two resolution steps against each other, this assumption would break."]}, "sandbox/cost_tracker.py": {"path": "sandbox/cost_tracker.py", "tier": "tier0", "oneLiner": "Tracks running $ cost per API call from pricing_table.yaml and enforces a run's cost ceiling.", "overview": ["Looks up a per-(provider, model_id, modality) $/1k-token rate from <code>pricing_table.yaml</code>, computes the cost of one call, adds it to a running total, and raises if that total has reached or exceeded the run's <code>max_cost_usd</code>.", "It exists to make runaway API spend impossible to miss: it never falls back to an estimated or default rate for a pricing entry it doesn't recognize — it fails loudly instead, consistent with the codebase's broader \"fail before spending budget\" philosophy.", "Called synchronously from <code>ModelGateway.generate()</code> after every successful LLM call (<code>record()</code> is deliberately a plain synchronous method, not <code>async def</code>, even though its only caller is async — this was a deliberate Phase 1 decision that must not be changed to add an <code>await</code>)."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/models.py"], "classes": [{"name": "CostCeilingExceeded", "purpose": "Raised by CostTracker.record() when the running total reaches/exceeds the run's max_cost_usd.", "attributes": [{"name": "current", "type": "float", "desc": "Total cost after the triggering call was counted."}, {"name": "ceiling", "type": "float", "desc": "The run's configured max_cost_usd."}]}, {"name": "CostTracker", "purpose": "Owns the running $ total for one run and enforces its cost ceiling.", "attributes": [{"name": "total_usd", "type": "float (property)", "desc": "The running total, read-only from outside."}], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, run: ExperimentRun, pricing_table_path: Path = Path(\"pricing_table.yaml\")):", "input": [{"name": "run", "type": "ExperimentRun", "desc": "Supplies max_cost_usd."}, {"name": "pricing_table_path", "type": "Path", "desc": "Defaults to the repo-root pricing_table.yaml; raises FileNotFoundError immediately if missing."}]}, "methods": [{"name": "record", "signature": "def record(self, provider: str, model_id: str, modality: str, prompt_tokens: int, completion_tokens: int) -> None:", "behavior": "Looks up the rate, computes <code>cost = (prompt_tokens/1000)*prompt_per_1k + (completion_tokens/1000)*completion_per_1k</code>, adds it to <code>total_usd</code> under a <code>threading.Lock</code>, then — <strong>only after that addition</strong> — raises <code>CostCeilingExceeded</code> if the new total has reached or exceeded <code>max_cost_usd</code>. The call that pushes the total over the ceiling is always counted; this is a deliberate design choice (per <code>full_design_doc.md</code> §7.3), not a bug — checking beforehand would require estimating a call's cost before its actual completion-token count is known.", "input": [{"name": "provider", "type": "str", "desc": "e.g. \"openai\"."}, {"name": "model_id", "type": "str", "desc": "e.g. \"gpt-4o\"."}, {"name": "modality", "type": "str", "desc": "\"text\" or \"vision\"."}, {"name": "prompt_tokens", "type": "int", "desc": ""}, {"name": "completion_tokens", "type": "int", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "None", "desc": "Mutates internal state; raises on ceiling breach."}, "notes": "Uses a plain <code>threading.Lock</code>, not <code>asyncio.Lock</code>, because <code>record()</code> is synchronous and contains no <code>await</code> point — under asyncio's cooperative scheduling this makes it already atomic with respect to other coroutines; the lock is defense-in-depth against a future refactor, not a requirement of the current control flow."}, {"name": "_lookup_rate", "signature": "def _lookup_rate(self, provider: str, model_id: str, modality: str) -> dict:", "behavior": "Raises ValueError (never a silent default) if the (provider, model_id, modality) triple has no entry in pricing_table.yaml.", "input": [{"name": "provider", "type": "str", "desc": ""}, {"name": "model_id", "type": "str", "desc": ""}, {"name": "modality", "type": "str", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "dict", "desc": "{prompt_per_1k: float, completion_per_1k: float}"}}]}]}, "sandbox/rate_limiter.py": {"path": "sandbox/rate_limiter.py", "tier": "tier0", "oneLiner": "Per-provider token-bucket-by-interval throttling, shared across all concurrent dispatch tasks in a run.", "overview": ["Enforces a minimum interval between consecutive requests to the same provider, computed from a requests-per-minute limit, using one <code>asyncio.Lock</code> per configured provider.", "It exists to keep the simulation's concurrent dispatch (up to <code>M</code> agents calling their model backend in the same turn) within each provider's actual rate limits, without needing per-call manual throttling logic scattered elsewhere.", "An unconfigured provider (e.g. a <code>local</code> backend with no entry in <code>ExperimentRun.rate_limits</code>) is treated as having no limit at all, not an error — a deliberate edge-case choice.", "Called from <code>ModelGateway.generate()</code> as an acquire/release pair around every dispatched call."], "dependencies": [], "classes": [{"name": "RateLimiter", "purpose": "One instance shared across all concurrent dispatch tasks for a run.", "attributes": [], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, limits: dict[str, int]):", "input": [{"name": "limits", "type": "dict[str, int]", "desc": "provider name -> requests/minute. A limit of 0 is treated as \"no limit\", not \"no requests allowed\" — almost certainly a config mistake otherwise, so it's guarded explicitly rather than causing a division-by-zero."}]}, "methods": [{"name": "acquire", "signature": "async def acquire(self, provider: str) -> None:", "behavior": "If <code>provider</code> isn't in the configured limits, returns immediately with no throttling. Otherwise, under that provider's <code>asyncio.Lock</code>, computes how long has elapsed since the last request to that provider and <code>await asyncio.sleep()</code>s the remainder of the minimum interval if needed, then records the new \"last request time\".", "input": [{"name": "provider", "type": "str", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "None", "desc": "Returns (possibly after sleeping) once it's safe to dispatch."}}, {"name": "release", "signature": "def release(self, provider: str) -> None:", "behavior": "Intentionally a no-op — a token-bucket-by-interval strategy needs no explicit release step. Kept only for interface symmetry with ModelGateway's acquire/release call site.", "input": [{"name": "provider", "type": "str", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "None", "desc": "No-op."}}]}]}, "sandbox/agent_manager.py": {"path": "sandbox/agent_manager.py", "tier": "tier1", "oneLiner": "Creates, holds, and mutates the Agent population for a run; owns memory_window/stance_history maintenance.", "overview": ["Creates the <code>run.M</code> agents for a run (persona + initial stance + shared language/model config), holds them in an internal dict keyed by <code>agent_id</code>, and is the only module that mutates an agent's <code>stance_history</code>/<code>memory_window</code> after a turn completes.", "It exists as the single owner of agent state so that no other module needs its own copy of \"what does the population currently look like\" — <code>interaction_engine.py</code> reads agents passed to it, and the eventual Orchestrator will call <code>apply_interaction()</code> once per successfully-processed agent-turn to advance state.", "Resolves a design gap the source documents left open (<code>plan.md</code>'s \"Question C1\"): <code>memory_window</code> is implemented as the agent's own most recent up-to-5 <code>interaction_id</code>s (a bounded pointer into its own <code>stance_history</code>), recomputed on every <code>apply_interaction()</code> call — not a record of which neighbor posts it saw.", "Depends only on <code>sandbox/models.py</code>."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/models.py"], "classes": [{"name": "AgentManager", "purpose": "Owns the Agent population dict for one run; the only module permitted to mutate agent state.", "attributes": [], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, run: ExperimentRun, rng: random.Random):", "input": [{"name": "run", "type": "ExperimentRun", "desc": "Supplies M, persona_pool_id, language_condition, model_backend_id, stance_scale."}, {"name": "rng", "type": "random.Random", "desc": "Should be seed_manager's persona_assignment_rng for reproducibility."}]}, "methods": [{"name": "initialize_population", "signature": "def initialize_population(self) -> list[Agent]:", "behavior": "Loads the persona pool (via <code>_load_persona_pool</code>), then for <code>i</code> in <code>range(run.M)</code>: assigns <code>personas[i % len(personas)]</code> (cycling if M exceeds the pool size), draws an <code>initial_stance</code> uniformly from <code>run.stance_scale</code>, and constructs an <code>Agent(agent_id=f\"agent_{i:04d}\", ...)</code> with empty <code>stance_history</code>/<code>memory_window</code> and <code>created_at_turn=0</code>. Stores each agent in the internal dict and returns the full list. Deterministic given the same seed: persona assignment and stance draws consume <code>self._rng</code> in a fixed order (persona first, then stance) for every agent.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "The M newly created agents, in creation order."}}, {"name": "_load_persona_pool", "signature": "def _load_persona_pool(self) -> list[str]:", "behavior": "Reads <code>data/personas/{persona_pool_id}.jsonl</code> as plain text lines (not JSON). Raises <code>FileNotFoundError</code> if the file is missing — should never happen since <code>config_loader.py</code> already validated this path exists, but this method does not trust that check blindly.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "list[str]", "desc": "One persona string per non-blank line."}}, {"name": "_draw_initial_stance", "signature": "def _draw_initial_stance(self) -> float:", "behavior": "Uniform draw via self._rng.choice(scale) — never the global random module, so reproducibility depends on the caller passing a seeded instance.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "float", "desc": "A value drawn from run.stance_scale."}}, {"name": "get_agent", "signature": "def get_agent(self, agent_id: str) -> Agent:", "behavior": "Raises KeyError, uncaught, if agent_id is unknown — treated as a programmer error, not defensively caught.", "input": [{"name": "agent_id", "type": "str", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "Agent", "desc": "The matching agent."}}, {"name": "all_agents", "signature": "def all_agents(self) -> list[Agent]:", "behavior": "Plain list() over the internal dict's values.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "Every agent currently held, in dict-insertion order."}}, {"name": "apply_interaction", "signature": "def apply_interaction(self, agent_id: str, interaction: Interaction) -> None:", "behavior": "Appends a new <code>StanceRecord(turn=interaction.turn, stance_value=interaction.stance_after, reason_text=interaction.reason_text, interaction_id=interaction.interaction_id)</code> to the agent's <code>stance_history</code>, then recomputes <code>memory_window</code> as <code>[r.interaction_id for r in agent.stance_history[-5:]]</code> — the agent's own most recent up to 5 interaction ids.", "input": [{"name": "agent_id", "type": "str", "desc": "Which agent to update."}, {"name": "interaction", "type": "Interaction", "desc": "The completed turn's record."}], "output": {"type": "None", "desc": "Mutates the agent in place."}}, {"name": "snapshot", "signature": "def snapshot(self) -> list[Agent]:", "behavior": "For checkpointing: copy.deepcopy(self.all_agents()), so later mutation of the manager's own agents never affects the returned snapshot.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "A deep copy of all_agents()."}}, {"name": "restore_from_snapshot", "signature": "def restore_from_snapshot(self, snapshot: list[Agent]) -> None:", "behavior": "Rebuilds the internal dict from a deep copy of the given list, so later mutation of the manager never affects the passed-in list either.", "input": [{"name": "snapshot", "type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "Typically a prior snapshot() result, or a CheckpointState.agent_snapshot loaded from disk."}], "output": {"type": "None", "desc": "Replaces internal state."}}]}]}, "sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py": {"path": "sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py", "tier": "tier1", "oneLiner": "Loads a meme dataset and decides, per scheduled speaker per turn, whether that speaker's post is a meme instead of generated text.", "overview": ["Loads a <code>data/memes/{meme_pool_id}.jsonl</code> pool into <code>MemeContent</code> records at construction (only if <code>config.enabled</code>), then, once per turn, decides for every scheduled speaker whether their post this turn should be a randomly-sampled meme rather than an LLM-generated response.", "It exists as the mechanism behind RQ3 (does meme presence accelerate polarization convergence): a meme-bearing agent's turn uses a dataset stance label directly instead of a model call, and is then sampled by the normal echo-chamber neighbor-selection mechanism exactly like any other agent's post — this module has no notion of \"who sees this meme later,\" only \"does this agent's post become a meme right now.\"", "Depends only on <code>sandbox/models.py</code>. Must be constructed with the same <code>rng</code> instance <code>seed_manager.py</code> provides (<code>meme_injection_rng</code>) for the run, and its decisions must be resolved as part of the frozen-snapshot phase of a turn, before any dispatch begins."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/models.py"], "classes": [{"name": "MemePoolManager", "purpose": "Owns the loaded meme pool (if enabled) and the per-turn injection decision logic.", "attributes": [], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, config: MemeInjectionConfig, rng: random.Random):", "input": [{"name": "config", "type": "MemeInjectionConfig", "desc": "If enabled, meme_pool_id must resolve to a real, non-empty pool file."}, {"name": "rng", "type": "random.Random", "desc": "Should be seed_manager's meme_injection_rng."}]}, "methods": [{"name": "_load_pool", "signature": "def _load_pool(self) -> list[MemeContent]:", "behavior": "Reads <code>data/memes/{meme_pool_id}.jsonl</code>, parsing each non-blank line via <code>MemeContent.model_validate_json()</code>. Raises <code>FileNotFoundError</code> if the file is missing, or <code>ValueError</code> if the file parses to zero items — both at construction time, before the run starts.", "input": [], "output": {"type": "list[MemeContent]", "desc": "Every non-blank line of the pool file, parsed."}}, {"name": "resolve_injections_for_turn", "signature": "def resolve_injections_for_turn(self, scheduled_speakers: list[Agent], turn: int) -> dict[str, MemeContent | None]:", "behavior": "If <code>config.enabled</code> is False, returns <code>None</code> for every speaker regardless of <code>injection_rate</code>. Otherwise, determines turn eligibility via <code>_is_eligible_turn</code> (always eligible under <code>\"random\"</code>; only the configured <code>fixed_turns</code> under <code>\"fixed_turn\"</code>), then for each speaker independently draws <code>self._rng.random() < injection_rate</code> to decide meme vs. None, sampling a random pool item via <code>_sample_meme</code> when a meme is chosen.", "input": [{"name": "scheduled_speakers", "type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "The agents scheduled to post this turn (in the current build, all agents)."}, {"name": "turn", "type": "int", "desc": "The current turn number."}], "output": {"type": "dict[str, MemeContent | None]", "desc": "agent_id -> the MemeContent it should post, or None to generate text normally."}, "notes": "Must be called with the same rng instance across a run, and as part of the frozen-snapshot phase of the (not-yet-built) Orchestrator's per-turn sequence — before any dispatch begins — so injection decisions never depend on any agent's in-progress turn-t output."}, {"name": "_is_eligible_turn", "signature": "def _is_eligible_turn(self, turn: int) -> bool:", "behavior": "\"random\" schedule: always True. \"fixed_turn\" schedule: True iff turn is in config.fixed_turns. Any other schedule value raises ValueError (defense-in-depth; Pydantic should already have rejected it).", "input": [{"name": "turn", "type": "int", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "bool", "desc": ""}}, {"name": "_sample_meme", "signature": "def _sample_meme(self) -> MemeContent:", "behavior": "self._rng.choice(self._pool).", "input": [], "output": {"type": "MemeContent", "desc": "A uniformly-random item from the loaded pool."}}]}]}, "sandbox/model_gateway.py": {"path": "sandbox/model_gateway.py", "tier": "tier1", "oneLiner": "The single normalized async interface to every LLM provider, backed by LiteLLM — rate limiting, retry, cost tracking.", "overview": ["Wraps <code>litellm.acompletion()</code> behind one uniform <code>async def generate()</code> call, so every other module deals with one provider-agnostic interface regardless of which backend a given run actually uses.", "It exists to concentrate every cross-cutting dispatch concern — rate-limit acquisition, retry-with-backoff on transient errors, distinguishing retryable vs. fatal provider errors, and cost recording — in one place, so no other module needs to know about LiteLLM, HTTP retries, or provider-specific exception types.", "Vision support is resolved via a <strong>static lookup table</strong> (<code>VISION_CAPABLE</code> / <code>TEXT_ONLY</code>), not a runtime capability probe, checked once at construction — an unrecognized <code>model_backend_id</code> raises immediately rather than silently defaulting to text-only.", "Depends on <code>sandbox/cost_tracker.py</code> and <code>sandbox/rate_limiter.py</code> (both Tier 0), plus the external <code>litellm</code> and <code>tenacity</code> packages."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/cost_tracker.py", "sandbox/rate_limiter.py"], "classes": [{"name": "TransientGatewayError", "purpose": "Wraps any provider error judged retryable (rate limits, connection errors). Drives tenacity's retry policy on _call_with_retry.", "attributes": []}, {"name": "FatalGatewayError", "purpose": "Wraps any provider error judged non-retryable (auth failure, bad request/invalid model, content policy rejection) — never retried.", "attributes": []}, {"name": "BackendResponse", "purpose": "Normalized dataclass returned by generate() regardless of which provider handled the call.", "attributes": [{"name": "text", "type": "str", "desc": "The model's raw completion text."}, {"name": "prompt_tokens", "type": "int", "desc": ""}, {"name": "completion_tokens", "type": "int", "desc": ""}, {"name": "latency_ms", "type": "int", "desc": ""}, {"name": "raw_provider_response", "type": "dict", "desc": "The full provider response, dumped via raw.model_dump() — kept for audit/debugging."}]}, {"name": "ModelGateway", "purpose": "The per-backend dispatch object: one instance per model_backend_id, shared across all agents using that backend.", "attributes": [{"name": "model_backend_id", "type": "str", "desc": ""}, {"name": "supports_vision", "type": "bool", "desc": "Resolved once at construction via _resolve_vision_support."}], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, model_backend_id: str, rate_limiter: RateLimiter, cost_tracker: CostTracker):", "input": [{"name": "model_backend_id", "type": "str", "desc": "e.g. \"gpt-4o\". Raises ValueError immediately if unrecognized by the vision lookup table."}, {"name": "rate_limiter", "type": "RateLimiter", "desc": "Shared across all dispatch for the run."}, {"name": "cost_tracker", "type": "CostTracker", "desc": "Shared across all dispatch for the run."}]}, "methods": [{"name": "generate", "signature": "async def generate(self, prompt_text: str, image: bytes | None = None, temperature: float = 0.7) -> BackendResponse:", "behavior": "Acquires the rate limiter for this backend's provider, calls <code>_call_with_retry</code> inside a <code>try/finally</code> that always releases the rate limiter afterward (even on exception), then records cost via <code>cost_tracker.record()</code> — called as a plain synchronous call, never <code>await</code>ed — with <code>modality=\"vision\"</code> if <code>image is not None</code> else <code>\"text\"</code>.", "input": [{"name": "prompt_text", "type": "str", "desc": ""}, {"name": "image", "type": "bytes | None", "desc": "If provided while supports_vision is False, the CALLER is responsible for having already substituted a caption-only prompt via vision_fallback.py — this method does not perform that substitution itself, it only reports supports_vision."}, {"name": "temperature", "type": "float, default 0.7", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "BackendResponse", "desc": "The normalized response."}}, {"name": "_call_with_retry", "signature": "@retry(retry=retry_if_exception_type(TransientGatewayError), stop=stop_after_attempt(3), wait=wait_exponential(multiplier=1, min=2, max=30), reraise=True)\nasync def _call_with_retry(self, prompt_text, image, temperature) -> BackendResponse:", "behavior": "Calls <code>litellm.acompletion()</code>. Maps <code>litellm.exceptions.RateLimitError</code> and <code>APIConnectionError</code> to <code>TransientGatewayError</code> (tenacity retries these, up to 3 total attempts, exponential backoff 2s-30s). Maps <code>AuthenticationError</code> and <code>BadRequestError</code> to <code>FatalGatewayError</code> (tenacity's retry predicate excludes this type, so it propagates on the first attempt). On success, builds a <code>BackendResponse</code> from <code>raw.choices[0].message.content</code>, <code>raw.usage.prompt_tokens</code>/<code>completion_tokens</code>, <code>raw.response_ms</code>, and <code>raw.model_dump()</code>.", "input": [{"name": "prompt_text", "type": "str", "desc": ""}, {"name": "image", "type": "bytes | None", "desc": ""}, {"name": "temperature", "type": "float", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "BackendResponse", "desc": ""}}, {"name": "_provider_name", "signature": "def _provider_name(self) -> str:", "behavior": "Splits model_backend_id on \"/\" if present; otherwise defaults to \"openai\".", "input": [], "output": {"type": "str", "desc": "The provider prefix, e.g. \"openai\"."}}]}], "functions": [{"name": "_resolve_vision_support", "signature": "def _resolve_vision_support(model_backend_id: str) -> bool:", "behavior": "Static lookup against two module-level sets: <code>VISION_CAPABLE = {\"gpt-4o\", \"gpt-4o-mini\", \"claude-sonnet-4-6\", \"gemini-2.0-flash\", \"llava\", \"qwen-vl\"}</code> and <code>TEXT_ONLY = {\"gpt-3.5-turbo\", \"llama-3.1-8b\", \"llama-3.1-70b\"}</code> (matched against the base name after any \"/\" prefix is stripped). Raises <code>ValueError</code> for any other <code>model_backend_id</code> — never silently defaults to False, since that could misclassify a vision-capable model as text-only without anyone noticing.", "input": [{"name": "model_backend_id", "type": "str", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "bool", "desc": "True if vision-capable, False if text-only."}, "notes": "<code>llava</code>/<code>qwen-vl</code> are recognized here as vision-capable (per the HLD's mention of local vision models) even though <code>pricing_table.yaml</code> has no pricing entry for them yet — using either in a real run would surface loudly via <code>CostTracker</code>'s \"no pricing entry\" <code>ValueError</code>, not silently misclassify them."}, {"name": "_build_messages", "signature": "def _build_messages(prompt_text: str, image: bytes | None) -> list[dict]:", "behavior": "If <code>image</code> is <code>None</code>, returns a single text-only user message. Otherwise base64-encodes the image and returns a multimodal user message with both a text part and an <code>image_url</code> part using a <code>data:image/jpeg;base64,...</code> URI.", "input": [{"name": "prompt_text", "type": "str", "desc": ""}, {"name": "image", "type": "bytes | None", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "list[dict]", "desc": "OpenAI-style chat \"messages\" array."}}]}, "sandbox/interaction_engine.py": {"path": "sandbox/interaction_engine.py", "tier": "tier2", "oneLiner": "Ohagi's alpha-sampling mechanism: blends uniform-random and stance-similarity-weighted neighbor selection.", "overview": ["Selects the N neighbors a speaking agent \"sees\" this turn, via a tunable <code>alpha</code> parameter: <code>alpha=0</code> is uniform random sampling, <code>alpha=1</code> is maximally homophilous (always prefers the closest-stance candidates), with continuous blending in between.", "It exists as the tunable echo-chamber mechanism the whole research design is built around — RQ1/RQ2/RQ3 all hold <code>alpha</code> fixed per run and compare conditions (language, meme presence) at that fixed homophily strength.", "Defines a <code>RecommendationStrategy</code> <code>Protocol</code> so the (not-yet-built) Orchestrator can accept any neighbor-selection strategy; <code>AlphaSampling</code> is the only concrete implementation that exists.", "Depends only on <code>sandbox/models.py</code> (for <code>Agent</code>)."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/models.py"], "classes": [{"name": "RecommendationStrategy", "purpose": "A typing.Protocol describing the contract any neighbor-selection strategy must satisfy: select_neighbors() must return exactly N distinct agents, never including the speaker itself.", "attributes": []}, {"name": "AlphaSampling", "purpose": "Ohagi's mechanism, implementing RecommendationStrategy.", "attributes": [{"name": "alpha", "type": "float", "desc": "Stored from construction."}, {"name": "N", "type": "int", "desc": "Stored from construction."}], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, alpha: float, N: int):", "input": [{"name": "alpha", "type": "float", "desc": "Must be in [0.0, 1.0]; raises ValueError otherwise."}, {"name": "N", "type": "int", "desc": "Must be >= 1; raises ValueError otherwise."}]}, "methods": [{"name": "select_neighbors", "signature": "def select_neighbors(self, speaker: Agent, all_agents: list[Agent], turn: int, rng: random.Random) -> list[Agent]:", "behavior": "Builds the candidate pool (all agents except the speaker), raising <code>ValueError</code> if fewer than N candidates remain. For each candidate, computes <code>distance = abs(current_stance(speaker) - current_stance(candidate))</code>, a similarity weight <code>1/(1+distance)</code>, and blends it with a uniform weight of 1.0 as <code>alpha * similarity_weight + (1-alpha) * uniform_weight</code>. Passes those weights to <code>_weighted_sample_without_replacement</code> to draw exactly N candidates.", "input": [{"name": "speaker", "type": "Agent", "desc": "The agent whose neighbors are being chosen."}, {"name": "all_agents", "type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "The full population."}, {"name": "turn", "type": "int", "desc": "Current turn number, used for stance lookup."}, {"name": "rng", "type": "random.Random", "desc": "Should be seed_manager's neighbor_sampling_rng."}], "output": {"type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "Exactly N distinct agents, never including speaker."}}]}], "functions": [{"name": "_current_stance", "signature": "def _current_stance(agent: Agent, turn: int) -> float:", "behavior": "turn==1 or an empty stance_history reads initial_stance; otherwise reads stance_history[-1].stance_value.", "input": [{"name": "agent", "type": "Agent", "desc": ""}, {"name": "turn", "type": "int", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "float", "desc": "The agent's stance as of the end of turn-1 (the frozen snapshot)."}, "notes": "Deliberately duplicates <code>Agent.current_stance()</code>'s exact logic rather than calling that method — a documented fidelity-to-spec choice (the design doc's own sample code never routes through <code>Agent.current_stance()</code>), not an accidental divergence."}, {"name": "_weighted_sample_without_replacement", "signature": "def _weighted_sample_without_replacement(items: list[Agent], weights: list[float], k: int, rng: random.Random) -> list[Agent]:", "behavior": "Efraimidis-Spirakis weighted reservoir sampling: keys each item as <code>rng.random() ** (1/weight)</code>, sorts descending by that key, and returns the top <code>k</code> items — O(n log k), fully deterministic given rng's state.", "input": [{"name": "items", "type": "list[Agent]", "desc": ""}, {"name": "weights", "type": "list[float]", "desc": ""}, {"name": "k", "type": "int", "desc": ""}, {"name": "rng", "type": "random.Random", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "k items, sampled without replacement, weighted."}}]}, "sandbox/stance_parser.py": {"path": "sandbox/stance_parser.py", "tier": "tier2", "oneLiner": "Pure functions extracting (stance_value, reason_text) from raw model output, and validating it against the configured stance scale.", "overview": ["Regex-matches a required <code>\"STANCE: <number>\"</code> line in a model's raw completion text, returning the numeric value plus the remaining text as the reasoning.", "It exists as the parsing boundary between free-text LLM output and the structured <code>stance_after</code>/<code>reason_text</code> fields an <code>Interaction</code> record needs — and as the single place that enforces \"never fabricate a placeholder stance\": both parse failure and an out-of-scale value raise the same exception type rather than being silently coerced to something plausible.", "Deliberately has <strong>no retry logic and no I/O</strong> — pure, stateless functions. Retry orchestration (re-dispatching to the Model Gateway with an amended prompt) is explicitly the job of the not-yet-built Orchestrator, which is documented to call these functions up to 3 times per agent-turn.", "Has no dependencies on any other <code>sandbox/*.py</code> module — only the stdlib <code>re</code>."], "dependencies": [], "classes": [{"name": "StanceParseFailure", "purpose": "Raised on any parse failure or out-of-scale value. Caught only by the Orchestrator, never by direct callers of these functions.", "attributes": []}], "functions": [{"name": "parse_stance", "signature": "def parse_stance(raw_text: str) -> tuple[float, str]:", "behavior": "Searches for the pattern <code>STANCE:\\s*(-?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)</code> (case-insensitive). Raises <code>StanceParseFailure</code> if no match is found, or if the matched group doesn't parse as a float. <code>reason_text</code> is <code>raw_text</code> with <strong>every</strong> <code>\"STANCE: <number>\"</code> occurrence stripped (<code>re.sub</code> with no count replaces all matches, not just the one the value was read from) and surrounding whitespace trimmed. When multiple STANCE-like substrings are present, the value returned is from the <strong>first (leftmost) match</strong>, but every match is stripped from the returned reason text.", "input": [{"name": "raw_text", "type": "str", "desc": "The model's raw completion text."}], "output": {"type": "tuple[float, str]", "desc": "(stance_value, reason_text)."}}, {"name": "clamp_and_validate_scale", "signature": "def clamp_and_validate_scale(value: float, stance_scale: list[float]) -> float:", "behavior": "Raises <code>StanceParseFailure</code> if <code>value</code> falls outside <code>[min(stance_scale), max(stance_scale)]</code>. Despite the name, it never actually clamps — an out-of-range value is treated identically to an unparseable one (both raise), per the \"never fabricate a placeholder stance\" principle.", "input": [{"name": "value", "type": "float", "desc": "A parsed stance value."}, {"name": "stance_scale", "type": "list[float]", "desc": "The run's configured scale, e.g. [1,2,3,4,5,6,7]."}], "output": {"type": "float", "desc": "value, unchanged, if it passes validation."}}]}, "sandbox/vision_fallback.py": {"path": "sandbox/vision_fallback.py", "tier": "tier2", "oneLiner": "The only place in the codebase that constructs a meme-derived prompt — same instruction framing regardless of receiver vision support, only the image payload differs.", "overview": ["Given a <code>MemeContent</code> and whether the receiving agent's backend supports vision, builds either a multimodal prompt (image bytes + caption framing) or a caption-only text prompt with the same instruction wording.", "It exists so a text-only-backend agent can still meaningfully react to a meme-bearing neighbor's post: instead of silently dropping the meme's content, its caption is woven into the prompt text with an explicit framing sentence.", "Depends only on <code>sandbox/models.py</code> (for <code>MemeContent</code>) and the stdlib <code>pathlib</code>."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/models.py"], "functions": [{"name": "build_meme_prompt", "signature": "def build_meme_prompt(meme: MemeContent, receiver_supports_vision: bool) -> tuple[str, bytes | None]:", "behavior": "If <code>receiver_supports_vision</code> is True: loads the image bytes via <code>_load_image</code> and returns a prompt text that frames the caption as accompanying a separately-shown image, plus the image bytes. If False: returns a prompt text that weaves the caption directly into the instruction text as \"Content (text-only, as no image is available to you): ...\", and <strong>never touches the filesystem</strong> in this branch — <code>_load_image</code> is only called on the vision-capable path.", "input": [{"name": "meme", "type": "MemeContent", "desc": "The meme content being shown to the receiver."}, {"name": "receiver_supports_vision", "type": "bool", "desc": "The receiving agent's backend's vision capability."}], "output": {"type": "tuple[str, bytes | None]", "desc": "(prompt_text, image_bytes_or_None)."}}, {"name": "_load_image", "signature": "def _load_image(image_path: str) -> bytes:", "behavior": "Raises FileNotFoundError, uncaught, if the path doesn't exist — treated as a data-integrity problem with the meme pool, not something to silently degrade around.", "input": [{"name": "image_path", "type": "str", "desc": "From MemeContent.image_path."}], "output": {"type": "bytes", "desc": "The raw file contents."}}]}, "sandbox/logging_writer.py": {"path": "sandbox/logging_writer.py", "tier": "tier2", "oneLiner": "Append-only JSONL persistence for one run's interactions.jsonl, run_config.json, and agents_final.jsonl.", "overview": ["Writes the three flat-file outputs that make up a completed (or in-progress) run's directory: an append-only <code>interactions.jsonl</code> (one line per agent-turn, concurrency-safe), a single-shot <code>run_config.json</code>, and a single-shot, overwriting <code>agents_final.jsonl</code>.", "It exists as the single, append-only, single-process persistence layer — disk-write failures (<code>OSError</code>, e.g. disk full) are allowed to propagate uncaught, since silently losing an <code>Interaction</code> record would corrupt a run's data integrity in a way no downstream analysis could detect.", "Does <strong>not</strong> create its output directory itself — unlike <code>checkpoint_manager.py</code>, which does <code>mkdir</code> its own subdirectory, <code>LoggingWriter</code> assumes <code>run_dir</code> already exists (the not-yet-built Orchestrator is expected to create it); calling any write method against a missing <code>run_dir</code> raises <code>FileNotFoundError</code> exactly like any other disk-write failure.", "Depends only on <code>sandbox/models.py</code>."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/models.py"], "classes": [{"name": "LoggingWriter", "purpose": "One instance per run, bound to that run's output directory.", "attributes": [], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, run_dir: Path):", "input": [{"name": "run_dir", "type": "Path", "desc": "The run's output directory; not created by this constructor."}]}, "methods": [{"name": "write_interaction", "signature": "async def write_interaction(self, interaction: Interaction) -> None:", "behavior": "Appends <code>interaction.model_dump_json() + \"\\n\"</code> under an internal <code>asyncio.Lock</code>, so concurrent dispatch tasks writing to the same open file handle within one process never interleave or tear a line — Python's async file writes are not guaranteed atomic across concurrent tasks, so this lock is what actually provides that guarantee (this is a single-process design; there is no cross-process write contention to handle).", "input": [{"name": "interaction", "type": "Interaction", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "None", "desc": "Appends one line to interactions.jsonl."}}, {"name": "write_run_config", "signature": "def write_run_config(self, run: ExperimentRun) -> None:", "behavior": "Called once at run start, before any concurrent activity begins — no locking needed. Writes run.model_dump_json(indent=2).", "input": [{"name": "run", "type": "ExperimentRun", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "None", "desc": "Writes run_config.json, overwriting if present."}}, {"name": "write_agents_final", "signature": "def write_agents_final(self, agents: list[Agent]) -> None:", "behavior": "Called once at run completion, after all turns finish and no further concurrent writes are possible — no locking needed. Opens the file in <code>\"w\"</code> mode (overwrite, not append), writing one <code>agent.model_dump_json()</code> line per agent — a second call with a different agent list leaves only that second list's contents.", "input": [{"name": "agents", "type": "list[Agent]", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "None", "desc": "Writes agents_final.jsonl."}}]}]}, "sandbox/checkpoint_manager.py": {"path": "sandbox/checkpoint_manager.py", "tier": "tier2", "oneLiner": "Per-turn checkpoint save/load with atomic rename, so a failed run can resume instead of restarting.", "overview": ["Saves the full agent population's state after each completed turn to a single overwritten checkpoint file, using a write-to-<code>.tmp</code>-then-atomic-rename pattern so a mid-write crash never leaves a torn/corrupt checkpoint on disk.", "It exists so a run interrupted partway through (crash, manual interrupt, cost ceiling breach) doesn't have to restart from turn 1 and re-spend already-completed API budget — only the <strong>latest</strong> checkpoint is ever kept, unlike the append-only <code>interactions.jsonl</code>.", "A checkpoint that exists but fails Pydantic schema validation on load raises uncaught, treated as a fatal resume failure requiring manual intervention — it never silently falls back to turn 0, which would discard completed work.", "Depends only on <code>sandbox/models.py</code> (for <code>Agent</code>, <code>CheckpointState</code>)."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/models.py"], "classes": [{"name": "CheckpointManager", "purpose": "Owns checkpoint save/load for all runs under one runs/ directory.", "attributes": [], "constructor_": {"signature": "def __init__(self, runs_dir: Path = Path(\"runs\")):", "input": [{"name": "runs_dir", "type": "Path", "desc": "Defaults to the repo-root runs/ directory."}]}, "methods": [{"name": "save", "signature": "def save(self, run_id: str, turn: int, agent_snapshot: list[Agent]) -> None:", "behavior": "Creates <code>runs/{run_id}/checkpoints/</code> if it doesn't exist (<code>mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)</code>). Builds a <code>CheckpointState(run_id, last_completed_turn=turn, agent_snapshot)</code>, writes its JSON to <code>latest.json.tmp</code>, then calls <code>tmp_path.replace(final_path)</code> — an atomic rename on POSIX, so <code>load()</code> will only ever see either the previous complete checkpoint or the fully-written new one, never a partial write.", "input": [{"name": "run_id", "type": "str", "desc": ""}, {"name": "turn", "type": "int", "desc": "The just-completed turn number."}, {"name": "agent_snapshot", "type": "list[Agent]", "desc": "Typically AgentManager.snapshot()'s output."}], "output": {"type": "None", "desc": "Writes runs/{run_id}/checkpoints/latest.json, overwriting any prior checkpoint."}}, {"name": "load", "signature": "def load(self, run_id: str) -> CheckpointState | None:", "behavior": "Returns <code>None</code> if <code>latest.json</code> doesn't exist. Otherwise parses it via <code>CheckpointState.model_validate_json()</code> — a malformed or schema-invalid checkpoint raises <code>pydantic.ValidationError</code> uncaught, not silently discarded.", "input": [{"name": "run_id", "type": "str", "desc": ""}], "output": {"type": "CheckpointState | None", "desc": "None if no checkpoint exists for this run_id (fresh run)."}}]}]}, "pyproject.toml": {"path": "pyproject.toml", "tier": "config", "oneLiner": "Package metadata, runtime/dev dependencies, and pytest configuration for the sandbox package.", "overview": ["Declares the installable package (<code>name = \"sandbox\"</code>, <code>requires-python = \">=3.11\"</code>), its runtime dependencies (<code>pydantic>=2.6</code>, <code>pyyaml>=6.0</code>, <code>litellm>=1.40</code>, <code>tenacity>=8.2</code>, <code>pandas>=2.2</code>, <code>statsmodels>=0.14</code>), and an optional <code>dev</code> extra (<code>pytest>=8.0</code>, <code>pytest-asyncio>=0.23</code>).", "<code>pandas</code> and <code>statsmodels</code> are pinned already even though no post-hoc analysis module exists yet — they're the planned dependencies of <code>stance_regression.py</code>/<code>bimodality_analysis.py</code>/etc. <code>litellm</code> and <code>tenacity</code> are consumed today only by <code>sandbox/model_gateway.py</code>.", "Sets <code>[tool.pytest.ini_options] asyncio_mode = \"auto\"</code>, so every <code>async def test_*</code> function across the test suite runs without needing an explicit <code>@pytest.mark.asyncio</code> decorator.", "Build backend is plain <code>setuptools</code> with <code>packages.find.include = [\"sandbox*\"]</code>."], "dependencies": []}, "pricing_table.yaml": {"path": "pricing_table.yaml", "tier": "config", "oneLiner": "Hand-maintained $-per-1k-token pricing, keyed provider -> model_id -> modality, read by CostTracker.", "overview": ["A hand-maintained YAML table of <code>{prompt_per_1k, completion_per_1k}</code> dollar rates, keyed <code>provider -> model_id -> modality</code> (<code>text</code> or <code>vision</code>), for every model this codebase currently recognizes.", "Its own header comment states the model ids are <strong>illustrative placeholders carried over from the design documents, not a confirmed final model selection</strong> — this table must be updated manually once real models are chosen for an actual research run, and manually whenever a provider changes its pricing (it is not derived from anything else).", "Read once at <code>CostTracker</code> construction; a lookup miss for any <code>(provider, model_id, modality)</code> triple raises <code>ValueError</code> rather than falling back to an estimate.", "Current entries: OpenAI (<code>gpt-4o</code>, <code>gpt-4o-mini</code>, <code>gpt-3.5-turbo</code>), Anthropic (<code>claude-sonnet-4-6</code>), Google (<code>gemini-2.0-flash</code>), and two zero-cost <code>local</code> entries (<code>llama-3.1-70b</code>, <code>llama-3.1-8b</code>, self-hosted). Note that <code>model_gateway.py</code>'s vision-capability table also recognizes <code>llava</code>/<code>qwen-vl</code> as vision-capable, but neither has a pricing entry here yet — using either would raise at cost-recording time."], "dependencies": [], "dependents": ["sandbox/cost_tracker.py"]}, "data/personas/test_pool.jsonl": {"path": "data/personas/test_pool.jsonl", "tier": "data", "oneLiner": "4-line plain-text persona pool, the default fixture used by most of the test suite.", "overview": ["Four plain-text lines (not JSON-wrapped), each one free-text persona description, e.g. \"A skeptical retail worker who distrusts institutions and values plain talk.\"", "Used as the default <code>persona_pool_id: \"test_pool\"</code> across <code>tests/conftest.py</code>'s <code>valid_config_dict</code> fixture and most other test modules' hand-built <code>ExperimentRun</code>s."], "dependencies": [], "dependents": ["sandbox/agent_manager.py"]}, "data/personas/pool_20.jsonl": {"path": "data/personas/pool_20.jsonl", "tier": "data", "oneLiner": "20-line persona pool, used specifically to exercise AgentManager's pool-cycling behavior at M=100.", "overview": ["20 plain-text persona lines. Exists specifically for <code>test_agent_manager.py::test_initialize_population_cycles_persona_pool</code>, which builds a run with <code>M=100</code> against this 20-entry pool and asserts each agent's persona equals <code>pool[i % 20]</code> — i.e. the pool is reused (cycled) 5 times over."], "dependencies": [], "dependents": ["sandbox/agent_manager.py"]}, "data/memes/test_pool.jsonl": {"path": "data/memes/test_pool.jsonl", "tier": "data", "oneLiner": "3-item MemeContent fixture pool used by meme_pool_manager.py's and vision_fallback.py's tests.", "overview": ["Three JSON lines, each a <code>MemeContent</code> record with fields <code>meme_id</code>, <code>image_path</code>, <code>caption_text</code>, <code>stance_label</code> (roughly on the same 1-7-ish scale the test suite's <code>stance_scale</code> uses), <code>offensiveness_label</code>, and <code>source_dataset: \"test_fixture_v1\"</code>.", "<code>image_path</code> fields point at <code>data/memes/images/test_00{1,2,3}.jpg</code> — only <code>test_001.jpg</code> actually exists on disk today; the other two are unused by any current test (no test loads meme_test_002 or meme_test_003's image)."], "dependencies": [], "dependents": ["sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py", "sandbox/vision_fallback.py"]}, "data/memes/empty_pool.jsonl": {"path": "data/memes/empty_pool.jsonl", "tier": "data", "oneLiner": "Zero-line file, deliberately empty, exercising MemePoolManager's empty-pool ValueError path.", "overview": ["An intentionally empty file. Its sole purpose is <code>test_meme_pool_manager.py::test_empty_pool_file_raises_value_error_at_construction</code>, which points a <code>MemeInjectionConfig</code> at <code>meme_pool_id=\"empty_pool\"</code> and asserts that constructing a <code>MemePoolManager</code> against it raises <code>ValueError</code> (not silently proceeding with an empty pool)."], "dependencies": [], "dependents": ["sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py"]}, "data/memes/images/test_001.jpg": {"path": "data/memes/images/test_001.jpg", "tier": "data", "oneLiner": "A tiny real JPEG file, the only meme image that actually exists on disk in this repository.", "overview": ["A small real JPEG binary. It exists specifically so <code>vision_fallback.py</code>'s vision-capable success path (<code>build_meme_prompt(..., receiver_supports_vision=True)</code>) has real bytes to read and return, rather than needing a mocked filesystem in <code>test_vision_fallback.py</code>.", "This is a binary asset, not a text/source file — it has no functions or classes to document."], "dependencies": [], "dependents": ["sandbox/vision_fallback.py"]}, "README.md": {"path": "README.md", "tier": "doc", "oneLiner": "One-line pointer to the architecture diagram image (agentic-network.png).", "overview": ["A minimal README consisting of a single \"Architecture Diagram\" heading and an embedded image reference to <code>agentic-network.png</code> at the repo root. It contains no setup instructions, usage examples, or other content — <code>CLAUDE.md</code> is the actual source of build/run/test instructions for this repository."], "dependencies": []}, "CLAUDE.md": {"path": "CLAUDE.md", "tier": "doc", "oneLiner": "Instructions for AI coding agents (Claude Code) working in this repository — architecture summary, commands, and invariants.", "overview": ["Project-specific guidance consumed by AI coding assistants: what the project is (three research questions, one simulation mode), how to run tests (<code>python -m pytest</code>), the strict dependency-tier build order, and a set of \"key design invariants\" that recur across the codebase (never silently clamp invalid input; seeded RNGs only, never the global <code>random</code> module; fatal vs. per-agent-recoverable error handling; <code>CostTracker.record()</code> stays synchronous; Pydantic v2 models throughout; vision support is a static lookup table).", "This documentation site's own accuracy requirements and structure were themselves derived by reading every file this document points at."], "dependencies": []}, "plan.md": {"path": "plan.md", "tier": "doc", "oneLiner": "Phase 2 build log: plans agent_manager.py, meme_pool_manager.py, model_gateway.py (Tier 1) before they were implemented. Merged/completed.", "overview": ["The planning document for Phase 2 of the build — the three Tier 1 modules (<code>agent_manager.py</code>, <code>meme_pool_manager.py</code>, <code>model_gateway.py</code>). Written and merged before that code existed; the code in the repository today matches this plan.", "Notably resolves \"Question C1\" — how <code>memory_window</code> and <code>apply_interaction()</code> should actually behave, since no source document fully specified it — by proposing (and the shipped code implements) <code>memory_window</code> as the agent's own most recent up-to-5 interaction ids.", "Also pins the vision/text-only model lookup table that <code>model_gateway.py</code>'s <code>_resolve_vision_support</code> implements, and lays out the acceptance-criteria tests each module needed — matched closely by the actual <code>tests/test_agent_manager.py</code>, <code>test_meme_pool_manager.py</code>, <code>test_model_gateway.py</code> files."], "dependencies": []}, "phase3.md": {"path": "phase3.md", "tier": "doc", "oneLiner": "Phase 3 build log: plans the five Tier 2 modules before they were implemented. Merged/completed; also flags the still-open prompt_builder.py design gap.", "overview": ["The planning document for Phase 3 — the five Tier 2 \"leaf\" modules (<code>interaction_engine.py</code>, <code>stance_parser.py</code>, <code>vision_fallback.py</code>, <code>logging_writer.py</code>, <code>checkpoint_manager.py</code>) that depend only on Tier 0/1 and not on each other. Written and merged before that code existed; the shipped code matches this plan closely, including its exact build ordering rationale.", "Notes that <code>sandbox_feature_specs.md</code> (referenced by <code>plan.md</code>'s Phase 2 feature numbering) does not actually exist anywhere in this repository, so this plan is scoped directly off <code>full_design_doc.md</code>'s own module list rather than off unverifiable feature numbers.", "<strong>Flags the single largest known gap in the codebase</strong>: <code>prompt_builder.py</code> is referenced by <code>full_design_doc.md</code>'s sample <code>simulation_orchestrator.py</code> code (as a constructor argument calling <code>build_discussion_prompt(agent, neighbors, turn, emphasize_format=...)</code>) but its actual design — prompt template, how persona/language/memory/neighbor posts get woven together — is specified nowhere. This is stated as the central open question blocking Phase 4 (<code>simulation_orchestrator.py</code>)."], "dependencies": []}, "Architecture-docs/sandbox_hld.md": {"path": "Architecture-docs/sandbox_hld.md", "tier": "doc", "oneLiner": "The system-level design specification: components, data model, module table, and three rounds of adversarial self-critique (Fixes A-N).", "overview": ["The stable, authoritative high-level design document. Defines the six-component system architecture (Config Loader, Orchestrator, Agent Manager, Interaction Engine, Meme Pool Manager, Model Backend layer, Logging layer, Post-hoc Analysis), the full dataclass-level schema (superseded in code by the Pydantic models in <code>sandbox/models.py</code>), and a table of every module to build mapped to which research question(s) depend on it.", "Its most distinctive content is three passes of adversarial self-critique against its own design (\"Critique Pass 1/2/3\"), each identifying a specific validity, scalability, or confound risk, resolved into a numbered list of Fixes (A through N) — e.g. Fix A (fixed 5-turn memory window, not token-budget-based, to avoid a language-driven truncation asymmetry), Fix F (the frozen-snapshot per-turn ordering guarantee), Fix M (deliberate seed reuse across language conditions so meme-injection patterns stay held constant while only language varies).", "Every built module's docstring cites one or more of these Fixes directly — when a design decision in the code looks arbitrary, this document is almost always where the rationale lives."], "dependencies": []}, "Architecture-docs/full_design_doc.md": {"path": "Architecture-docs/full_design_doc.md", "tier": "doc", "oneLiner": "The low-level design specification: per-module function signatures, error-handling contracts, concurrency notes, full schema, storage layout, and API design.", "overview": ["Goes one level deeper than the HLD: for every module (§3.1 through §3.14), gives real Python sample code with type hints, an explicit \"error handling\" paragraph, and an explicit \"concurrency\" paragraph. Every built <code>sandbox/*.py</code> module's own docstring says it is a \"direct port\" of a specific section here.", "§4 gives the complete Pydantic schema (matching <code>sandbox/models.py</code> exactly for every model that has been built). §5 gives the on-disk storage layout (<code>runs/{run_id}/...</code>) and worked JSONL examples. §6 designs a CLI (<code>python -m sandbox run/status/resume/list</code>) and Python API (<code>sandbox/api.py</code>'s <code>launch_run</code>, <code>get_run_status</code>, <code>load_run_dataframe</code>, <code>list_runs</code>) — <strong>none of which exist as code yet</strong> in this repository; §6 is a design only. §7 documents cross-cutting concerns (the full validation-rule list, logging conventions, the exact cost-ceiling-enforcement timing). §8 lists explicitly open, unresolved questions (meme stance-label rescaling, SeedManager's concurrency assumption, judge-model cost tracking for the not-yet-built coherence scorer).", "Contains the sample implementation of <code>simulation_orchestrator.py</code> (§3.9) — the central per-turn loop that would wire every other module together — which is the most important not-yet-implemented piece of this system; see the Pipelines and Architecture tabs for how this documentation site treats that gap."], "dependencies": []}, "tests/__init__.py": {"path": "tests/__init__.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Empty file marking tests/ as a package.", "overview": ["Empty — makes tests/ importable as a package. No content to document."], "dependencies": []}, "tests/conftest.py": {"path": "tests/conftest.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Shared pytest fixtures: a valid base config dict, and a helper to write a config dict to a temp YAML file.", "overview": ["Provides two fixtures consumed mainly by <code>test_config_loader.py</code> (and reusable anywhere): <code>valid_config_dict</code>, a minimal but fully valid <code>ExperimentRun</code>-shaped dict (M=10, N=3, K=2, alpha=0.5, <code>persona_pool_id=\"test_pool\"</code>, etc.), and <code>write_config</code>, a factory fixture that YAML-dumps a given dict to a file under pytest's <code>tmp_path</code> and returns its <code>Path</code>."], "dependencies": [], "functions": [{"name": "_base_config_dict", "signature": "def _base_config_dict() -> dict:", "behavior": "Returns a fresh dict literal with hard-coded valid values for every required ExperimentRun field except the ones with defaults (meme_injection, etc.).", "input": [], "output": {"type": "dict", "desc": "A minimal valid ExperimentRun-shaped config dict."}}]}, "tests/test_config_loader.py": {"path": "tests/test_config_loader.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies load_run_config()'s validation, error-accumulation, and git-hash-injection behavior.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/config_loader.py</code>'s <code>load_run_config()</code> against <code>tests/conftest.py</code>'s <code>valid_config_dict</code>/<code>write_config</code> fixtures."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/config_loader.py"], "testCoverage": ["A valid config produces an ExperimentRun with a 40-character git_commit_hash populated automatically.", "A user-supplied git_commit_hash in the YAML is ignored/overwritten.", "A missing file, and malformed YAML, both raise ConfigLoadError.", "A missing required field (e.g. topic) names that field in the error.", "N >= M is rejected.", "meme_injection.enabled=True without meme_pool_id is rejected before the filesystem check even runs.", "meme_injection pointing at a nonexistent pool names the resolved data/memes path in the error.", "meme_injection pointing at a real pool (test_pool) succeeds.", "Two independent errors (bad alpha + missing persona pool) both surface from one call.", "A persona pool missing alone is reported, naming the pool id.", "mode values other than \"multi_turn\" are rejected."]}, "tests/test_seed_manager.py": {"path": "tests/test_seed_manager.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies SeedManager's three RNG streams are reproducible, independent, and stateful.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/seed_manager.py</code>'s <code>SeedManager</code> directly, with no fixtures beyond plain seed integers."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/seed_manager.py"], "testCoverage": ["The same seed produces identical neighbor_sampling_rng draw sequences across two separate SeedManager instances.", "The same seed produces identical meme_injection_rng draw sequences across two separate instances.", "The three streams (neighbor/meme/persona) never produce identical draw sequences to each other, even from the same base seed.", "Each property returns the same random.Random instance by identity on repeated access, not a fresh one.", "Repeated access to the same property advances the stream (doesn't reset it) — consecutive draws differ."]}, "tests/test_cost_tracker.py": {"path": "tests/test_cost_tracker.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies cost computation, ceiling enforcement (after-the-fact), missing-pricing errors, and thread-safety of CostTracker.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/cost_tracker.py</code>'s <code>CostTracker</code> against the real repo-root <code>pricing_table.yaml</code> (not a mock), via a locally-built <code>_make_run()</code> helper."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/cost_tracker.py"], "testCoverage": ["record() computes the expected $ cost and accumulates it into total_usd.", "An unknown (provider, model, modality) combination raises ValueError and leaves total_usd at 0.", "CostCeilingExceeded is raised only after the triggering call's cost has already been added to total_usd.", "max_cost_usd=None never raises, regardless of accumulated total.", "Vision and text modality costs for the same model are tracked independently (and differently).", "Concurrent record() calls, run via asyncio.gather over asyncio.to_thread, lose no updates (validates the internal threading.Lock).", "A missing pricing_table_path raises FileNotFoundError at construction."]}, "tests/test_rate_limiter.py": {"path": "tests/test_rate_limiter.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies RateLimiter's interval spacing, unconfigured-provider passthrough, concurrent serialization, and the zero-limit edge case.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/rate_limiter.py</code>'s <code>RateLimiter</code> directly, using real (short) sleeps and wall-clock timing assertions rather than mocks."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/rate_limiter.py"], "testCoverage": ["acquire() spaces out consecutive calls to the same provider by at least the configured minimum interval.", "An unconfigured provider (\"local\", never in the limits dict) returns immediately with no throttling, even under a very tight limit on a different provider.", "Concurrent acquire() calls for the same provider (via asyncio.gather) still serialize correctly to the minimum interval.", "A limit of 0 is treated as \"no limit\" (fast, no division-by-zero), not \"zero requests allowed\".", "release() is a no-op for both a configured and an unconfigured provider — never raises."]}, "tests/test_agent_manager.py": {"path": "tests/test_agent_manager.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies population initialization (persona cycling, seeded reproducibility), get_agent's KeyError contract, and apply_interaction/snapshot/restore semantics.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/agent_manager.py</code>'s <code>AgentManager</code> via local <code>_make_run()</code>/<code>_make_interaction()</code> helpers, against the real <code>data/personas/test_pool.jsonl</code> and <code>pool_20.jsonl</code> fixtures."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/agent_manager.py"], "testCoverage": ["M=100 against a 20-entry pool (pool_20) cycles personas correctly (agent[i].persona == pool[i % 20]).", "Two managers seeded identically produce identical initial_stance sequences.", "get_agent() on an unknown id raises KeyError, uncaught.", "A missing persona pool raises FileNotFoundError at initialize_population() time.", "apply_interaction() called 7 times (more than the memory_window cap of 5) leaves stance_history at length 7 but memory_window capped at the most recent 5 interaction ids, and current_stance() reflects the latest turn.", "snapshot() is unaffected by mutation of the manager that happens after the snapshot was taken.", "restore_from_snapshot() reproduces agent state exactly, and further mutation after a restore does not leak back into the snapshot object that was passed in."]}, "tests/test_meme_pool_manager.py": {"path": "tests/test_meme_pool_manager.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies injection-rate/schedule decision logic, seeded reproducibility, and the empty/missing-pool error paths.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py</code>'s <code>MemePoolManager</code> against the real <code>data/memes/test_pool.jsonl</code> and <code>empty_pool.jsonl</code> fixtures."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py"], "testCoverage": ["enabled=False yields None for every speaker regardless of injection_rate.", "injection_rate=0.0 never injects, checked across many turns.", "injection_rate=1.0 with a \"random\" schedule always injects for every speaker.", "A \"fixed_turn\" schedule with fixed_turns={5} never injects except exactly on turn 5, even at injection_rate=1.0.", "Two managers with identically-seeded rng produce identical injection decisions (same meme_id per agent per turn) across an identical call sequence.", "An empty pool file raises ValueError at construction.", "A missing pool file raises FileNotFoundError at construction."]}, "tests/test_model_gateway.py": {"path": "tests/test_model_gateway.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies retry-on-transient-error, no-retry-on-fatal-error, vision lookup validation, cost-tracker call shape, and rate-limiter release guarantees — all against a mocked litellm.acompletion.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/model_gateway.py</code>'s <code>ModelGateway</code> with <code>litellm.acompletion</code> patched via <code>unittest.mock</code> (never a real network call), and <code>create_autospec</code> mocks for <code>RateLimiter</code>/<code>CostTracker</code>. An autouse fixture patches <code>asyncio.sleep</code> so tenacity's exponential backoff doesn't actually slow the test suite down."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/model_gateway.py"], "testCoverage": ["A RateLimitError followed by a successful response results in generate() succeeding on the 2nd attempt (mock_completion.call_count == 2).", "An AuthenticationError raises FatalGatewayError immediately, with exactly 1 attempt (no retry).", "An unrecognized model_backend_id raises ValueError at ModelGateway construction, before any generate() call.", "A text call (image=None) records cost with modality=\"text\".", "A vision call (image=bytes) records cost with modality=\"vision\".", "rate_limiter.release() is called exactly once on a successful call.", "rate_limiter.release() is called exactly once even when the underlying call raises FatalGatewayError (validates the try/finally)."]}, "tests/test_interaction_engine.py": {"path": "tests/test_interaction_engine.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies AlphaSampling's construction-time validation, alpha=0/alpha=1 boundary behavior, distinctness/never-self guarantees, and turn=1's initial_stance-only read.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/interaction_engine.py</code>'s <code>AlphaSampling</code> via a local <code>_make_agent()</code>/<code>_population()</code> helper — no file fixtures needed."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/interaction_engine.py"], "testCoverage": ["alpha outside [0,1], and N < 1, both raise ValueError at construction.", "alpha=1.0 with clearly-separated stances deterministically returns the N closest-stance candidates, verified across 10 different seeds.", "alpha=0.0's selection frequency across candidates is roughly uniform over 2000 trials with varying seeds (wide-tolerance statistical assertion).", "select_neighbors() never returns the speaker, and always returns exactly N distinct agents.", "A population smaller than N raises ValueError rather than returning a short list.", "Two calls with identically-seeded random.Random instances produce identical neighbor sets (same order, not just same set).", "turn=1 always reads initial_stance, even when the speaker already has stance_history entries present (distinguishes correct behavior from a hypothetical bug where turn 1 wrongly reads history)."]}, "tests/test_stance_parser.py": {"path": "tests/test_stance_parser.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies parse_stance()'s extraction/stripping behavior and clamp_and_validate_scale()'s range checking.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/stance_parser.py</code>'s two pure functions directly — no fixtures, no mocking."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/stance_parser.py"], "testCoverage": ["A well-formed \"STANCE: 5\\n...\" line parses to (5.0, reason) with the STANCE line stripped from reason_text.", "A missing STANCE line, and a non-numeric STANCE value, both raise StanceParseFailure.", "Negative and decimal values (\"STANCE: -2.5\") parse correctly.", "The pattern match is case-insensitive (\"stance: 3\" matches).", "With multiple STANCE-like substrings present, the FIRST (leftmost) match's value is returned, but re.sub strips every occurrence from reason_text (pins down actual regex behavior rather than assuming it).", "clamp_and_validate_scale(): a value inside [min,max] passes through unchanged; values below or above the range both raise StanceParseFailure."]}, "tests/test_vision_fallback.py": {"path": "tests/test_vision_fallback.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies build_meme_prompt()'s vision vs. caption-only branching, including that the caption-only path never touches the filesystem.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/vision_fallback.py</code>'s <code>build_meme_prompt()</code> against the real <code>data/memes/images/test_001.jpg</code> fixture."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/vision_fallback.py"], "testCoverage": ["A vision-capable receiver gets back image bytes that exactly match the real file's contents, and the caption text appears in the prompt.", "A text-only receiver gets image_bytes=None, with the caption text still woven into the prompt.", "A missing image file with a vision-capable receiver raises FileNotFoundError.", "A text-only receiver pointed at a nonexistent image path still succeeds — proving the caption-only branch never calls _load_image."]}, "tests/test_logging_writer.py": {"path": "tests/test_logging_writer.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies concurrent-write safety on interactions.jsonl, round-tripping of all three output files, agents_final's overwrite semantics, and the missing-run_dir error path.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/logging_writer.py</code>'s <code>LoggingWriter</code> against pytest's <code>tmp_path</code>, using real concurrency via <code>asyncio.gather</code> (not sequential calls) for the locking test."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/logging_writer.py"], "testCoverage": ["50 concurrent write_interaction() calls (via asyncio.gather) produce exactly 50 valid, non-torn JSON lines with the expected set of interaction_ids — the actual guarantee the internal asyncio.Lock exists to provide.", "write_run_config() produces a run_config.json that round-trips via ExperimentRun.model_validate_json() to an equal object.", "write_agents_final() writes exactly len(agents) lines, each round-tripping via Agent.model_validate_json().", "A second write_agents_final() call with a different agent list overwrites (not appends) — only the second list's contents remain.", "Calling write_run_config() against a run_dir that doesn't exist yet raises FileNotFoundError (confirms LoggingWriter does not create its own run_dir)."]}, "tests/test_checkpoint_manager.py": {"path": "tests/test_checkpoint_manager.py", "tier": "test", "oneLiner": "Verifies save/load round-tripping, overwrite-not-accumulate semantics, corrupted-checkpoint error propagation, directory auto-creation, and atomic-rename cleanup.", "overview": ["Exercises <code>sandbox/checkpoint_manager.py</code>'s <code>CheckpointManager</code> against pytest's <code>tmp_path</code>, using <code>AgentManager.snapshot()</code> output (via a local <code>_make_agent_snapshot()</code> helper) as realistic input — exactly what the eventual Orchestrator would pass."], "dependencies": ["sandbox/checkpoint_manager.py"], "testCoverage": ["load() on a run_id with no checkpoint directory returns None.", "save() then load() round-trips run_id, last_completed_turn, and the full agent_snapshot exactly.", "Two sequential save() calls at different turns for the same run_id: load() returns only the latest (confirms overwrite, not accumulation).", "A corrupted/truncated latest.json (written directly, bypassing save()) raises a Pydantic ValidationError, uncaught, on load().", "save() creates the checkpoints/ directory tree if it doesn't already exist.", "No .tmp file is left behind after a successful save() (confirms the atomic rename actually completed).", "The saved file's raw bytes are valid parseable JSON."]}}, "fileTree": [{"type": "folder", "name": "sandbox", "children": [{"type": "file", "name": "__init__.py", "key": "sandbox/__init__.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "models.py", "key": "sandbox/models.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "config_loader.py", "key": "sandbox/config_loader.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "seed_manager.py", "key": "sandbox/seed_manager.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "cost_tracker.py", "key": "sandbox/cost_tracker.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "rate_limiter.py", "key": "sandbox/rate_limiter.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "agent_manager.py", "key": "sandbox/agent_manager.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "meme_pool_manager.py", "key": "sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "model_gateway.py", "key": "sandbox/model_gateway.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "interaction_engine.py", "key": "sandbox/interaction_engine.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "stance_parser.py", "key": "sandbox/stance_parser.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "vision_fallback.py", "key": "sandbox/vision_fallback.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "logging_writer.py", "key": "sandbox/logging_writer.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "checkpoint_manager.py", "key": "sandbox/checkpoint_manager.py"}]}, {"type": "folder", "name": "tests", "children": [{"type": "file", "name": "__init__.py", "key": "tests/__init__.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "conftest.py", "key": "tests/conftest.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_config_loader.py", "key": "tests/test_config_loader.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_seed_manager.py", "key": "tests/test_seed_manager.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_cost_tracker.py", "key": "tests/test_cost_tracker.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_rate_limiter.py", "key": "tests/test_rate_limiter.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_agent_manager.py", "key": "tests/test_agent_manager.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_meme_pool_manager.py", "key": "tests/test_meme_pool_manager.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_model_gateway.py", "key": "tests/test_model_gateway.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_interaction_engine.py", "key": "tests/test_interaction_engine.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_stance_parser.py", "key": "tests/test_stance_parser.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_vision_fallback.py", "key": "tests/test_vision_fallback.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_logging_writer.py", "key": "tests/test_logging_writer.py"}, {"type": "file", "name": "test_checkpoint_manager.py", "key": "tests/test_checkpoint_manager.py"}]}, {"type": "folder", "name": "data", "children": [{"type": "folder", "name": "personas", "children": [{"type": "file", "name": "test_pool.jsonl", "key": "data/personas/test_pool.jsonl"}, {"type": "file", "name": "pool_20.jsonl", "key": "data/personas/pool_20.jsonl"}]}, {"type": "folder", "name": "memes", "children": [{"type": "file", "name": "test_pool.jsonl", "key": "data/memes/test_pool.jsonl"}, {"type": "file", "name": "empty_pool.jsonl", "key": "data/memes/empty_pool.jsonl"}, {"type": "folder", "name": "images", "children": [{"type": "file", "name": "test_001.jpg", "key": "data/memes/images/test_001.jpg"}]}]}]}, {"type": "folder", "name": "Architecture-docs", "children": [{"type": "file", "name": "sandbox_hld.md", "key": "Architecture-docs/sandbox_hld.md"}, {"type": "file", "name": "full_design_doc.md", "key": "Architecture-docs/full_design_doc.md"}]}, {"type": "folder", "name": "config & docs (root)", "children": [{"type": "file", "name": "pyproject.toml", "key": "pyproject.toml"}, {"type": "file", "name": "pricing_table.yaml", "key": "pricing_table.yaml"}, {"type": "file", "name": "plan.md", "key": "plan.md"}, {"type": "file", "name": "phase3.md", "key": "phase3.md"}, {"type": "file", "name": "README.md", "key": "README.md"}, {"type": "file", "name": "CLAUDE.md", "key": "CLAUDE.md"}]}], "filesIndexGroups": [{"title": "Tier 0 — pure data & standalone infrastructure", "description": "No dependency on each other; every other tier ultimately depends on these.", "keys": ["sandbox/models.py", "sandbox/config_loader.py", "sandbox/seed_manager.py", "sandbox/cost_tracker.py", "sandbox/rate_limiter.py"]}, {"title": "Tier 1 — depends only on Tier 0", "description": "", "keys": ["sandbox/agent_manager.py", "sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py", "sandbox/model_gateway.py"]}, {"title": "Tier 2 — depends only on Tier 0/1", "description": "The five most recently built modules; none depend on each other.", "keys": ["sandbox/interaction_engine.py", "sandbox/stance_parser.py", "sandbox/vision_fallback.py", "sandbox/logging_writer.py", "sandbox/checkpoint_manager.py"]}, {"title": "Package marker", "description": "", "keys": ["sandbox/__init__.py"]}, {"title": "Configuration", "description": "", "keys": ["pyproject.toml", "pricing_table.yaml"]}, {"title": "Data fixtures", "description": "Input assets under data/, used both by the test suite and by whatever eventually runs a real simulation.", "keys": ["data/personas/test_pool.jsonl", "data/personas/pool_20.jsonl", "data/memes/test_pool.jsonl", "data/memes/empty_pool.jsonl", "data/memes/images/test_001.jpg"]}, {"title": "Tests", "description": "One pytest module per sandbox/ module, plus shared fixtures.", "keys": ["tests/conftest.py", "tests/test_config_loader.py", "tests/test_seed_manager.py", "tests/test_cost_tracker.py", "tests/test_rate_limiter.py", "tests/test_agent_manager.py", "tests/test_meme_pool_manager.py", "tests/test_model_gateway.py", "tests/test_interaction_engine.py", "tests/test_stance_parser.py", "tests/test_vision_fallback.py", "tests/test_logging_writer.py", "tests/test_checkpoint_manager.py", "tests/__init__.py"]}, {"title": "Planning & design documents", "description": "The specification and build-log documents everything above is a direct port of.", "keys": ["Architecture-docs/sandbox_hld.md", "Architecture-docs/full_design_doc.md", "plan.md", "phase3.md", "README.md", "CLAUDE.md"]}], "architecture": {"intro": "The sandbox is built as strict, one-directional dependency tiers: a module may only depend on modules in a lower tier, never sideways within its own tier and never upward. <strong>Tiers 0, 1, and 2 (13 modules) are fully implemented and unit-tested today.</strong> Tier 3 — the integration layer that would actually run a simulation end-to-end — is <strong>designed in the architecture docs but not yet written as code</strong>; this tab documents those planned components too, clearly marked, because understanding what's missing is part of understanding the system's current shape. Component order below follows the dependency tiers, lowest first.", "components": [{"id": "config-loader", "name": "Config / Run Loader", "tierLabel": "Tier 0 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "The mandatory entry gate for every simulation run — a pure parse-and-validate function, not a class.", "whatItDoes": "Reads a YAML run config, validates it into an <code>ExperimentRun</code> Pydantic object, resolves the current git commit hash, and confirms every referenced persona/meme pool file exists on disk. Accumulates <em>all</em> errors found (both schema and filesystem) into one <code>ConfigLoadError</code> rather than failing on the first one, so a researcher sees every problem in a config in one pass.", "files": ["sandbox/config_loader.py"], "communicatesWith": ["sandbox/models.py (produces ExperimentRun)", "the local git repository (via subprocess)", "data/personas/, data/memes/ (existence checks only)"], "dataFlow": "YAML file on disk → validated ExperimentRun object, consumed by every constructor downstream (AgentManager, CostTracker, MemePoolManager, ...)."}, {"id": "data-models", "name": "Data Model Layer", "tierLabel": "Tier 0 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "The shared Pydantic v2 schema — not a running component, but the vocabulary every other component speaks.", "whatItDoes": "Defines <code>Agent</code>, <code>StanceRecord</code>, <code>MemeContent</code>, <code>Interaction</code>, <code>MemeInjectionConfig</code>, <code>ExperimentRun</code>, and <code>CheckpointState</code>, with schema-level validation (regex-constrained enums, cross-field <code>@model_validator</code>s, bounded list lengths) so that invalid data is rejected at construction, not discovered downstream.", "files": ["sandbox/models.py"], "communicatesWith": ["every other component in the system, directly or indirectly"], "dataFlow": "Sits underneath everything; has no data flow of its own beyond being instantiated, validated, and serialized (model_dump_json() / model_validate_json()) by its callers."}, {"id": "seed-manager", "name": "Seed Manager", "tierLabel": "Tier 0 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "Central RNG seeding for every non-LLM stochastic choice in the system.", "whatItDoes": "Given one base seed, hands out three independently-seeded, deterministically-offset <code>random.Random</code> streams — one each for neighbor sampling, meme injection, and persona assignment — so those three kinds of randomness never correlate with each other, and are fully reproducible given the same base seed.", "files": ["sandbox/seed_manager.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Agent Manager (persona_assignment_rng)", "Interaction/Recommendation Engine (neighbor_sampling_rng)", "Meme Pool Manager (meme_injection_rng)"], "dataFlow": "One integer seed in → three long-lived random.Random instances out, each consumed repeatedly across the run's lifetime by its designated component."}, {"id": "agent-manager", "name": "Agent Manager", "tierLabel": "Tier 1 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "Owns and mutates the Agent population — the single source of truth for \"what does the population currently look like\".", "whatItDoes": "Creates the run's M agents (persona + initial stance + shared language/model config) at population-initialization time, and is the only component permitted to update an agent's <code>stance_history</code>/<code>memory_window</code> after a turn (via <code>apply_interaction()</code>). Also owns snapshot/restore for checkpointing.", "files": ["sandbox/agent_manager.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Data Model Layer", "Seed Manager (consumes persona_assignment_rng)", "data/personas/*.jsonl", "Checkpoint Manager (via snapshot()/restore_from_snapshot())"], "dataFlow": "ExperimentRun + a persona pool file → M Agent objects. Later, one Interaction record per successful agent-turn flows back in via apply_interaction(), advancing each agent's stance_history/memory_window."}, {"id": "interaction-engine", "name": "Interaction / Recommendation Engine", "tierLabel": "Tier 2 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "The tunable echo-chamber mechanism — selects N neighbors per agent per turn.", "whatItDoes": "Implements Ohagi's alpha-sampling: blends uniform-random neighbor selection (<code>alpha=0</code>) with maximally stance-homophilous selection (<code>alpha=1</code>) via a weighted-reservoir sample. Exposes a <code>RecommendationStrategy</code> protocol so alternative strategies could be substituted later, though <code>AlphaSampling</code> is the only implementation that exists.", "files": ["sandbox/interaction_engine.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Data Model Layer (reads Agent stance state)", "Seed Manager (consumes neighbor_sampling_rng)"], "dataFlow": "The current agent population + a speaker + a turn number → exactly N distinct neighbor Agents, weighted by stance similarity to the speaker."}, {"id": "meme-pool-manager", "name": "Meme Pool Manager", "tierLabel": "Tier 1 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "Loads a labeled meme dataset and decides, per scheduled speaker per turn, whether that speaker's post is a meme instead of generated text.", "whatItDoes": "The mechanism behind RQ3. Loads <code>MemeContent</code> records from a <code>data/memes/*.jsonl</code> pool at construction (only if meme injection is enabled), then each turn independently decides per agent (at a configured rate, on either a random or fixed-turn schedule) whether to hand back a sampled <code>MemeContent</code> or <code>None</code>.", "files": ["sandbox/meme_pool_manager.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Data Model Layer", "Seed Manager (consumes meme_injection_rng)", "data/memes/*.jsonl"], "dataFlow": "A scheduled-speaker list + turn number → {agent_id: MemeContent | None}. A meme-selected agent's stance_after becomes the meme's fixed stance_label directly, with no model call at all."}, {"id": "model-gateway", "name": "Model Gateway", "tierLabel": "Tier 1 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "The single normalized async interface to every LLM provider — the AI/ML integration layer.", "whatItDoes": "Wraps <code>litellm.acompletion()</code> behind one uniform <code>async generate()</code> call. Resolves vision-vs-text-only capability via a static lookup table, acquires the shared rate limiter before dispatch, retries transient provider errors (rate limits, connection errors) with exponential backoff via <code>tenacity</code> while never retrying fatal ones (auth failures, bad requests), and records $ cost after every successful call.", "files": ["sandbox/model_gateway.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Rate Limiter (acquire/release)", "Cost Tracker (record)", "external LLM providers via litellm (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, local)"], "dataFlow": "A prompt (+ optional image bytes) → a normalized BackendResponse (text, token counts, latency, raw provider payload). Every text/vision speaker-turn call in the eventual simulation loop flows through here."}, {"id": "rate-limiter", "name": "Rate Limiter", "tierLabel": "Tier 0 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "Per-provider token-bucket-by-interval throttling, shared across all concurrent dispatch.", "whatItDoes": "Enforces a minimum spacing between consecutive requests to the same provider from a configured requests-per-minute limit, using one <code>asyncio.Lock</code> per provider. An unconfigured provider is treated as unlimited, not an error.", "files": ["sandbox/rate_limiter.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Model Gateway (called as an acquire/release pair around every dispatched call)"], "dataFlow": "A provider name in → either an immediate return or an await-sleep until the minimum interval has elapsed, then returns."}, {"id": "cost-tracker", "name": "Cost Tracker", "tierLabel": "Tier 0 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "Running $ cost accounting per call, with a hard ceiling.", "whatItDoes": "Looks up a $/1k-token rate from <code>pricing_table.yaml</code> keyed by (provider, model, modality), accumulates a running total under a thread lock, and raises once the run's <code>max_cost_usd</code> ceiling is reached — always counting the triggering call's own cost first.", "files": ["sandbox/cost_tracker.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Model Gateway (record() called after every successful dispatch)", "pricing_table.yaml"], "dataFlow": "(provider, model_id, modality, prompt_tokens, completion_tokens) → an updated running total_usd, and a possible CostCeilingExceeded exception."}, {"id": "stance-parser", "name": "Stance Parser", "tierLabel": "Tier 2 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "The parsing boundary between free-text LLM output and structured stance data.", "whatItDoes": "Pure, stateless functions: extracts a required <code>\"STANCE: <number>\"</code> line and the surrounding reasoning text from a model's raw completion, and validates the parsed value against the run's configured stance scale. Never retries and never fabricates a placeholder value — both failure modes raise the same <code>StanceParseFailure</code>.", "files": ["sandbox/stance_parser.py"], "communicatesWith": ["(consumed by whatever calls Model Gateway.generate() and needs to turn its text into a stance)"], "dataFlow": "Raw model completion text → (stance_value, reason_text), or a raised StanceParseFailure that the (not-yet-built) Orchestrator is documented to catch and retry around."}, {"id": "vision-fallback", "name": "Vision Fallback", "tierLabel": "Tier 2 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "The only place in the codebase that constructs a meme-derived prompt.", "whatItDoes": "Given a meme and whether its receiver's backend supports vision, builds either a multimodal prompt (image bytes + caption framing) or a caption-only text prompt using identical instruction wording — so a text-only receiver still meaningfully sees the meme's content rather than it being silently dropped.", "files": ["sandbox/vision_fallback.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Data Model Layer (MemeContent)", "data/memes/images/*.jpg"], "dataFlow": "A MemeContent + a boolean vision flag → (prompt_text, image_bytes_or_None), fed into a subsequent Model Gateway call."}, {"id": "logging-writer", "name": "Logging / Persistence Layer", "tierLabel": "Tier 2 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "Append-only, concurrency-safe JSONL persistence for one run's output.", "whatItDoes": "Writes <code>interactions.jsonl</code> (append-only, one line per agent-turn, serialized under an <code>asyncio.Lock</code> so concurrent dispatch tasks never interleave a write), plus single-shot <code>run_config.json</code> and overwriting <code>agents_final.jsonl</code>. Assumes its output directory already exists; does not create it.", "files": ["sandbox/logging_writer.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Data Model Layer (Agent, ExperimentRun, Interaction)", "runs/{run_id}/ on disk"], "dataFlow": "One Interaction/ExperimentRun/Agent-list object at a time → one or more JSON(L) lines appended or written to a run's output directory."}, {"id": "checkpoint-manager", "name": "Checkpoint Manager", "tierLabel": "Tier 2 · Implemented", "whatItIs": "Per-turn checkpoint save/load, so an interrupted run can resume instead of restart.", "whatItDoes": "Saves the full agent population's serialized state after each turn to a single overwritten file, using a write-to-.tmp-then-atomic-rename pattern so a crash mid-write never corrupts the checkpoint. A malformed checkpoint on load raises rather than silently resuming from turn 0.", "files": ["sandbox/checkpoint_manager.py"], "communicatesWith": ["Agent Manager (snapshot()/restore_from_snapshot() round-trip through here)", "runs/{run_id}/checkpoints/ on disk"], "dataFlow": "A run_id + turn number + agent snapshot → runs/{run_id}/checkpoints/latest.json; on resume, that file → a CheckpointState handed back to Agent Manager."}, {"id": "orchestrator", "name": "Simulation Orchestrator", "tierLabel": "Tier 3 · PLANNED — not implemented", "whatItIs": "The integration tier. Designed in detail in <code>full_design_doc.md</code> §3.9 (a full sample <code>SimulationOrchestrator</code> class with <code>run()</code>/<code>_run_turn()</code>/<code>_process_one_agent_turn()</code>), but <strong>no <code>sandbox/simulation_orchestrator.py</code> file exists in this repository yet.</strong>", "whatItDoes": "As designed: the only module that would call every other component in sequence, driving the K-turn loop. Each turn: freeze the current agent snapshot (implicit — no writes have happened yet) → resolve neighbor assignments for all M agents via the Interaction Engine → resolve meme-injection assignments via the Meme Pool Manager → dispatch concurrently (generated-text speakers to the Model Gateway with stance-parser retry, meme speakers as a free lookup) → write each result via the Logging Writer and apply it via the Agent Manager → checkpoint → next turn. This exact ordering (neighbor/meme resolution strictly before any dispatch) is referred to throughout the docs as \"Fix F\" and is load-bearing for reproducibility.", "files": [], "communicatesWith": ["Agent Manager", "Interaction Engine", "Meme Pool Manager", "Model Gateway", "Stance Parser", "Vision Fallback", "Logging Writer", "Checkpoint Manager", "Prompt Builder (also planned)"], "dataFlow": "ExperimentRun → a fully executed, checkpointed, logged simulation run. This is the central data flow of the entire system and currently exists only as design-doc sample code, not as runnable code."}, {"id": "prompt-builder", "name": "Prompt Builder", "tierLabel": "Tier 3 · PLANNED — undesigned", "whatItIs": "Referenced by the Orchestrator's sample code (<code>self._prompt_builder.build_discussion_prompt(agent, neighbors, turn, emphasize_format=...)</code>) but its actual design does not exist anywhere — no prompt template, no specification of how persona/language/memory/neighbor posts get woven into text.", "whatItDoes": "As referenced (not designed): would construct the actual text/multimodal prompt sent to a model for a given agent's turn, incorporating persona, recent memory (via <code>memory_window</code>), and sampled neighbors' most recent posts (including meme content, handled via Vision Fallback).", "files": [], "communicatesWith": ["Simulation Orchestrator (would be its sole caller)"], "dataFlow": "phase3.md explicitly names this the central open question blocking the Orchestrator's implementation — no data flow can be documented beyond the one call signature referenced in the design doc's sample code."}, {"id": "posthoc-analysis", "name": "Post-hoc Analysis Module", "tierLabel": "Planned — not implemented", "whatItIs": "Designed in <code>full_design_doc.md</code> §3.13 as six modules (<code>stance_regression.py</code>, <code>coherence_scorer.py</code>, <code>codemix_ratio_tracker.py</code>, <code>sentiment_proxy.py</code>, <code>bimodality_analysis.py</code>, <code>embedding_cluster.py</code>), none of which exist as code yet.", "whatItDoes": "As designed: offline scripts, run after a simulation completes, that load <code>interactions.jsonl</code> into a pandas DataFrame (via a shared <code>load_run_dataframe()</code> loader) and compute a specific metric — Ohagi-style OLS regression (RQ1), LLM-judge coherence scoring filtered to generated-text-only rows (RQ2), code-mixing ratio, sentiment/emotion scoring, bimodality/convergence-speed classification (RQ1 secondary, RQ3 primary), and Sentence-BERT embedding clustering.", "files": [], "communicatesWith": ["interactions.jsonl (read-only, offline — no dependency on the Orchestrator itself, only on its output format)"], "dataFlow": "A completed run's interactions.jsonl → regression coefficients / coherence scores / bimodality classifications, entirely offline and with no simulation calls of its own."}, {"id": "cli-api", "name": "CLI + Python API", "tierLabel": "Planned — not implemented", "whatItIs": "Designed in <code>full_design_doc.md</code> §6 (a <code>python -m sandbox run/status/resume/list</code> CLI and a <code>sandbox/api.py</code> with <code>launch_run</code>/<code>get_run_status</code>/<code>load_run_dataframe</code>/<code>list_runs</code>), plus an optional run-manifest SQLite index and an optional local HTTP status endpoint — <strong>none of this exists as code</strong>; there is no <code>sandbox/api.py</code>, no <code>__main__.py</code>, no CLI entry point anywhere in the repository.", "whatItDoes": "As designed: the human-facing entry point a researcher would actually use — validate and launch a run, check its progress, resume an interrupted one, list runs by filter, and (via the Python API) pull a run's data into a notebook for analysis.", "files": [], "communicatesWith": ["Config Loader", "Simulation Orchestrator (fully blocked on this not existing)"], "dataFlow": "A YAML config path (CLI) or run_id (status/resume/list) in → a launched/queried run, or a pandas DataFrame, out. Fully blocked on the Orchestrator existing."}, {"id": "external-providers", "name": "External Model Providers", "tierLabel": "External dependency", "whatItIs": "Not part of this codebase — the actual LLM backends the Model Gateway dispatches to via LiteLLM.", "whatItDoes": "OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, and self-hosted/local backends (per <code>pricing_table.yaml</code>'s current entries: gpt-4o family, claude-sonnet-4-6, gemini-2.0-flash, llama-3.1 variants). The pricing table's own header notes these model ids are illustrative placeholders, not a confirmed final model selection.", "files": [], "communicatesWith": ["Model Gateway (the only component that ever calls out to them, via litellm.acompletion)"], "dataFlow": "A normalized messages payload out → a raw provider completion response back, immediately normalized into a BackendResponse by the Model Gateway."}]}, "pipelines": [{"id": "config-validation", "name": "Config Validation Pipeline", "status": "tier0", "description": "The mandatory first step of every run, traced directly from <code>config_loader.load_run_config()</code>. Turns a researcher-authored YAML file into a validated <code>ExperimentRun</code>, or fails loudly with every problem found listed at once. Fully implemented and unit-tested (<code>tests/test_config_loader.py</code>).", "plantuml": "@startuml\nactor Researcher\nparticipant \"load_run_config()\" as Loader\nparticipant \"yaml.safe_load\" as YAML\nparticipant \"ExperimentRun (pydantic)\" as Model\nparticipant \"_resolve_git_commit_hash()\" as Git\nparticipant \"_referenced_asset_errors()\" as Assets\ndatabase \"data/personas/*.jsonl\\ndata/memes/*.jsonl\" as Disk\n\nResearcher -> Loader: load_run_config(path)\nLoader -> Loader: check path.exists()\nLoader -> YAML: safe_load(path.read_text())\nYAML --> Loader: raw dict\nLoader -> Git: _resolve_git_commit_hash()\nGit --> Loader: git_commit_hash (or ConfigLoadError)\nLoader -> Model: ExperimentRun(**raw)\nModel --> Loader: validated run OR ValidationError (collected, not raised yet)\nLoader -> Assets: _referenced_asset_errors(raw)\nAssets -> Disk: check persona_pool_id / meme_pool_id exist\nDisk --> Assets: exists / missing\nAssets --> Loader: list[str] missing-asset errors\nalt any errors collected\n    Loader --> Researcher: raise ConfigLoadError(all errors)\nelse no errors\n    Loader --> Researcher: return ExperimentRun\nend\n@enduml"}, {"id": "population-init", "name": "Population Initialization Pipeline", "status": "tier1", "description": "Traced from <code>AgentManager.initialize_population()</code>. Turns a validated run config plus a persona pool file into the M-agent population every other component operates on. Fully implemented and unit-tested (<code>tests/test_agent_manager.py</code>).", "plantuml": "@startuml\nparticipant Caller\nparticipant \"AgentManager\" as AM\ndatabase \"data/personas/{pool_id}.jsonl\" as Pool\nparticipant \"persona_assignment_rng\\n(random.Random)\" as RNG\nparticipant \"Agent (pydantic)\" as Agent\n\nCaller -> AM: initialize_population()\nAM -> Pool: _load_persona_pool()\nPool --> AM: list[str] personas\nloop i in range(run.M)\n    AM -> RNG: choice(stance_scale)  ' _draw_initial_stance\n    RNG --> AM: initial_stance\n    AM -> Agent: Agent(agent_id=f\"agent_{i:04d}\", persona=personas[i % len(personas)], ...)\n    Agent --> AM: new Agent\n    AM -> AM: store in self._agents dict\nend\nAM --> Caller: list[Agent] (length M)\n@enduml"}, {"id": "neighbor-sampling", "name": "Neighbor Sampling Pipeline (Alpha-Sampling)", "status": "tier2", "description": "Traced from <code>AlphaSampling.select_neighbors()</code>. The core echo-chamber mechanism: chooses which N agents a speaker \"sees\" this turn, blending uniform and stance-homophilous selection via a tunable alpha. Fully implemented and unit-tested (<code>tests/test_interaction_engine.py</code>).", "plantuml": "@startuml\nparticipant Caller\nparticipant \"AlphaSampling\" as AS\nparticipant \"_current_stance()\" as Stance\nparticipant \"_weighted_sample_without_replacement()\" as Sampler\n\nCaller -> AS: select_neighbors(speaker, all_agents, turn, rng)\nAS -> AS: candidates = all_agents minus speaker\nAS -> AS: check len(candidates) >= N (else ValueError)\nAS -> Stance: _current_stance(speaker, turn)\nStance --> AS: speaker's current stance\nloop for each candidate\n    AS -> Stance: _current_stance(candidate, turn)\n    Stance --> AS: candidate's current stance\n    AS -> AS: distance = abs(speaker_stance - candidate_stance)\\nweight = alpha*(1/(1+distance)) + (1-alpha)*1.0\nend\nAS -> Sampler: _weighted_sample_without_replacement(candidates, weights, N, rng)\nSampler --> AS: N distinct Agents\nAS --> Caller: list[Agent] (length N, never includes speaker)\n@enduml"}, {"id": "meme-injection", "name": "Meme Injection Decision Pipeline", "status": "tier1", "description": "Traced from <code>MemePoolManager.resolve_injections_for_turn()</code>. Decides, for every scheduled speaker in a turn, whether that agent's post is a meme drawn from a labeled dataset instead of a generated response. Fully implemented and unit-tested (<code>tests/test_meme_pool_manager.py</code>).", "plantuml": "@startuml\nparticipant Caller\nparticipant \"MemePoolManager\" as MPM\nparticipant \"meme_injection_rng\\n(random.Random)\" as RNG\ndatabase \"loaded MemeContent pool\" as Pool\n\nCaller -> MPM: resolve_injections_for_turn(scheduled_speakers, turn)\nalt config.enabled == False\n    MPM --> Caller: {agent_id: None for every speaker}\nelse config.enabled == True\n    MPM -> MPM: _is_eligible_turn(turn)\\n(always True for \"random\"; turn in fixed_turns for \"fixed_turn\")\n    loop for each speaker\n        alt eligible turn\n            MPM -> RNG: random()\n            RNG --> MPM: draw\n            alt draw < injection_rate\n                MPM -> Pool: _sample_meme() = rng.choice(pool)\n                Pool --> MPM: MemeContent\n                MPM -> MPM: result[agent_id] = MemeContent\n            else\n                MPM -> MPM: result[agent_id] = None\n            end\n        else not eligible\n            MPM -> MPM: result[agent_id] = None\n        end\n    end\n    MPM --> Caller: dict[agent_id, MemeContent | None]\nend\n@enduml"}, {"id": "model-dispatch", "name": "Model Dispatch Pipeline (Rate Limit → Retry → Cost Tracking)", "status": "tier1", "description": "Traced from <code>ModelGateway.generate()</code>, integrating three built modules: <code>RateLimiter</code>, <code>ModelGateway</code> itself (with its tenacity-based retry policy), and <code>CostTracker</code>. This is the one real, tested flow combining multiple Tier 0/1 modules together outside of a test file. Fully implemented and unit-tested against a mocked <code>litellm.acompletion</code> (<code>tests/test_model_gateway.py</code>).", "plantuml": "@startuml\nparticipant Caller\nparticipant \"ModelGateway\" as GW\nparticipant \"RateLimiter\" as RL\nparticipant \"litellm.acompletion\" as LiteLLM\nparticipant \"CostTracker\" as CT\n\nCaller -> GW: await generate(prompt_text, image, temperature)\nGW -> RL: await acquire(provider)\nRL --> GW: (returns once interval satisfied)\nGW -> GW: _call_with_retry(prompt_text, image, temperature)\nloop up to 3 attempts (tenacity, exponential backoff 2s-30s)\n    GW -> LiteLLM: acompletion(model, messages, temperature)\n    alt success\n        LiteLLM --> GW: raw response\n        GW -> GW: build BackendResponse\n    else RateLimitError / APIConnectionError\n        LiteLLM --> GW: exception\n        GW -> GW: raise TransientGatewayError (retried)\n    else AuthenticationError / BadRequestError\n        LiteLLM --> GW: exception\n        GW -> GW: raise FatalGatewayError (NOT retried)\n        GW --> Caller: propagate FatalGatewayError\n    end\nend\nGW -> RL: release(provider)  ' always runs, via try/finally\nGW -> CT: record(provider, model_id, modality, prompt_tokens, completion_tokens)\nalt total_usd >= max_cost_usd\n    CT --> GW: raise CostCeilingExceeded\n    GW --> Caller: propagate CostCeilingExceeded\nelse under ceiling\n    CT --> GW: (returns normally)\n    GW --> Caller: BackendResponse\nend\n@enduml"}, {"id": "stance-extraction", "name": "Stance Extraction Pipeline", "status": "tier2", "description": "Traced from <code>stance_parser.parse_stance()</code> and <code>clamp_and_validate_scale()</code>. Turns a model's free-text completion into a validated numeric stance plus reasoning text — the last step before an <code>Interaction</code> record can be built. Fully implemented and unit-tested (<code>tests/test_stance_parser.py</code>); has no retry logic of its own by design.", "plantuml": "@startuml\nparticipant Caller\nparticipant \"parse_stance()\" as Parse\nparticipant \"clamp_and_validate_scale()\" as Clamp\n\nCaller -> Parse: parse_stance(raw_text)\nParse -> Parse: regex search r\"STANCE:\\\\s*(-?\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?)\"\nalt no match found\n    Parse --> Caller: raise StanceParseFailure\nelse match found but not numeric\n    Parse --> Caller: raise StanceParseFailure\nelse match found and numeric\n    Parse -> Parse: reason = re.sub(pattern, \"\", raw_text).strip()\\n(strips EVERY match, not just the first)\n    Parse --> Caller: (stance_value, reason_text)\n    Caller -> Clamp: clamp_and_validate_scale(stance_value, run.stance_scale)\n    alt value outside [min(scale), max(scale)]\n        Clamp --> Caller: raise StanceParseFailure\n    else value in range\n        Clamp --> Caller: return value unchanged\n    end\nend\n@enduml"}, {"id": "vision-fallback-flow", "name": "Meme Prompt / Vision Fallback Pipeline", "status": "tier2", "description": "Traced from <code>vision_fallback.build_meme_prompt()</code>. Decides how a meme's content is presented to a receiving agent depending on that agent's backend's vision capability. Fully implemented and unit-tested (<code>tests/test_vision_fallback.py</code>).", "plantuml": "@startuml\nparticipant Caller\nparticipant \"build_meme_prompt()\" as BMP\nparticipant \"_load_image()\" as LoadImg\ndatabase \"data/memes/images/*.jpg\" as Images\n\nCaller -> BMP: build_meme_prompt(meme, receiver_supports_vision)\nalt receiver_supports_vision == True\n    BMP -> LoadImg: _load_image(meme.image_path)\n    LoadImg -> Images: path.read_bytes()\n    alt file missing\n        Images --> LoadImg: (does not exist)\n        LoadImg --> BMP: raise FileNotFoundError (uncaught)\n    else file exists\n        Images --> LoadImg: raw bytes\n        LoadImg --> BMP: image_bytes\n        BMP --> Caller: (prompt_text with \"[Image shown separately]\" framing, image_bytes)\n    end\nelse receiver_supports_vision == False\n    note right of BMP: filesystem is never touched on this branch\n    BMP --> Caller: (prompt_text with caption woven in as text, None)\nend\n@enduml"}, {"id": "interaction-logging", "name": "Interaction Logging Pipeline", "status": "tier2", "description": "Traced from <code>LoggingWriter.write_interaction()</code>. The concurrency-safe append path that every agent-turn's result flows through. Fully implemented and unit-tested under real <code>asyncio.gather</code> concurrency (<code>tests/test_logging_writer.py</code>).", "plantuml": "@startuml\nparticipant \"Dispatch task 1\" as T1\nparticipant \"Dispatch task 2\" as T2\nparticipant \"Dispatch task N\" as TN\nparticipant \"LoggingWriter\" as LW\nparticipant \"asyncio.Lock\" as Lock\ndatabase \"interactions.jsonl\" as File\n\npar concurrent dispatch tasks\n    T1 -> LW: await write_interaction(interaction_1)\n    T2 -> LW: await write_interaction(interaction_2)\n    TN -> LW: await write_interaction(interaction_n)\nend\nLW -> Lock: acquire (serializes actual writes)\nLW -> File: append interaction.model_dump_json() + \"\\n\"\nLW -> Lock: release\nnote right of File: N concurrent calls always produce\\nexactly N untorn, valid JSON lines\n@enduml"}, {"id": "checkpoint-resume", "name": "Checkpoint Save & Resume Pipeline", "status": "tier2", "description": "Traced from <code>CheckpointManager.save()</code>/<code>load()</code>. How a run's progress survives a crash or interruption. Fully implemented and unit-tested, including the corrupted-checkpoint error path (<code>tests/test_checkpoint_manager.py</code>).", "plantuml": "@startuml\nparticipant \"AgentManager\" as AM\nparticipant \"CheckpointManager\" as CM\ndatabase \"runs/{run_id}/checkpoints/latest.json\" as Latest\ndatabase \"runs/{run_id}/checkpoints/latest.json.tmp\" as Tmp\n\n== Save (after each completed turn) ==\nAM -> CM: save(run_id, turn, agent_manager.snapshot())\nCM -> CM: mkdir(checkpoints/, exist_ok=True)\nCM -> CM: build CheckpointState(run_id, last_completed_turn=turn, agent_snapshot)\nCM -> Tmp: write_text(state.model_dump_json())\nCM -> Latest: tmp_path.replace(final_path)  ' atomic rename on POSIX\nnote right of Latest: overwrites any previous checkpoint\\n(only the LATEST is ever kept)\n\n== Resume (at run start) ==\nparticipant Orchestrator as Orch\nOrch -> CM: load(run_id)\nCM -> Latest: check exists\nalt no checkpoint file\n    Latest --> CM: (does not exist)\n    CM --> Orch: None  ' fresh run, start at turn 1\nelse checkpoint exists\n    Latest --> CM: raw JSON\n    CM -> CM: CheckpointState.model_validate_json(raw)\n    alt schema-invalid / corrupted\n        CM --> Orch: raise pydantic.ValidationError (uncaught, fatal)\n    else valid\n        CM --> Orch: CheckpointState (resume from last_completed_turn + 1)\n    end\nend\n@enduml"}, {"id": "per-turn-loop", "name": "Per-Turn Simulation Loop (Full Orchestrated Run)", "status": "tier3", "description": "<strong>PLANNED — the Orchestrator module this diagram depicts does not exist as code in this repository.</strong> This is the central, integrating pipeline that the entire system is designed around, sourced directly from the sample <code>SimulationOrchestrator</code> implementation in <code>full_design_doc.md</code> §3.9 (which every built module's own docstring already refers to — e.g. <code>meme_pool_manager.py</code> and <code>agent_manager.py</code> both explicitly describe their role in this sequence). It is included here because every implemented module's design already assumes it, and because <code>phase3.md</code> names it — blocked specifically on the undesigned <code>prompt_builder.py</code> — as the very next piece of work. Every interaction shown below is between real classes that already exist; only the orchestrating class itself (<code>SimulationOrchestrator</code>) and <code>PromptBuilder</code> are not yet implemented.", "plantuml": "@startuml\nparticipant \"SimulationOrchestrator\\n(PLANNED)\" as Orch\nparticipant \"AgentManager\" as AM\nparticipant \"AlphaSampling\\n(interaction_engine.py)\" as IE\nparticipant \"MemePoolManager\" as MPM\nparticipant \"PromptBuilder\\n(PLANNED, undesigned)\" as PB\nparticipant \"ModelGateway\" as GW\nparticipant \"stance_parser\" as SP\nparticipant \"LoggingWriter\" as LW\nparticipant \"CheckpointManager\" as CM\n\nOrch -> CM: load(run_id)\nalt checkpoint exists\n    CM --> Orch: CheckpointState\n    Orch -> AM: restore_from_snapshot(state.agent_snapshot)\nelse fresh run\n    Orch -> AM: initialize_population()\n    Orch -> LW: write_run_config(run)\nend\n\nloop turn = start_turn .. K\n    == Step 1-2: freeze snapshot + resolve neighbors (sequential, no dispatch yet) ==\n    Orch -> AM: all_agents()\n    AM --> Orch: current population (the frozen snapshot)\n    loop for each agent\n        Orch -> IE: select_neighbors(agent, all_agents, turn, rng)\n        IE --> Orch: N neighbor Agents\n    end\n\n    == Step 3: resolve meme injections (still before any dispatch) ==\n    Orch -> MPM: resolve_injections_for_turn(all_agents, turn)\n    MPM --> Orch: {agent_id: MemeContent | None}\n\n    == Step 4-5: concurrent dispatch + collect (asyncio.gather, return_exceptions=True) ==\n    par for each agent concurrently\n        alt agent has a meme assigned\n            Orch -> Orch: build Interaction directly from meme.stance_label\\n(no Model Gateway call)\n        else agent generates text\n            Orch -> PB: build_discussion_prompt(agent, neighbors, turn)\n            PB --> Orch: prompt text\n            Orch -> GW: await generate(prompt, temperature)\n            GW --> Orch: BackendResponse\n            Orch -> SP: parse_stance(response.text)\n            alt StanceParseFailure\n                Orch -> PB: build_discussion_prompt(..., emphasize_format=True)\n                note right of Orch: retried up to 2 more times;\\nexhausted retries -> failed_logged_null Interaction\n            else FatalGatewayError\n                note right of Orch: not retried at all -> failed_logged_null Interaction\n            else success\n                Orch -> Orch: build success Interaction\n            end\n        end\n    end\n\n    == Step 6: advance snapshot ==\n    loop for each successful result\n        Orch -> LW: await write_interaction(interaction)\n        Orch -> AM: apply_interaction(agent_id, interaction)\n    end\n    Orch -> CM: save(run_id, turn, agent_manager.snapshot())\nend\n\nOrch -> LW: write_agents_final(agent_manager.all_agents())\n@enduml"}], "hld": {"sections": [{"title": "System purpose", "paragraphs": ["The sandbox simulates populations of LLM-backed agents discussing a topic over multiple turns under a tunable echo-chamber (homophilous neighbor-sampling) mechanism, to answer three research questions: whether Hindi-English code-mixed (\"Hinglish\") discussion produces different polarization dynamics than English discussion under identical conditions (<strong>RQ1</strong>); whether the quality of an agent's opinion-updating reasoning differs by language and correlates with polarization speed (<strong>RQ2</strong>, a post-hoc analysis of RQ1's own data); and whether injecting memes from a pre-existing labeled dataset into an ongoing discussion accelerates convergence to a polarized distribution compared to text-only discussion (<strong>RQ3</strong>).", "The single architectural fact that shapes everything in this system: there is exactly <strong>one simulation mode</strong> (multi-turn discussion), and memes are implemented as a <em>content-replacement mechanism</em> — a meme-bearing agent's turn uses a dataset-provided stance label instead of an LLM call, and that agent is then sampled by the same echo-chamber mechanism exactly like any other agent. This is what lets RQ1, RQ2, and RQ3 share one orchestrator, one schema family, and one config surface, with no cross-model sweep and no second execution path anywhere in the system."]}, {"title": "Current implementation status", "paragraphs": ["The system is being built bottom-up, one dependency tier per build phase, each planned in a Markdown document before being coded. <strong>Tier 0 (5 modules), Tier 1 (3 modules), and Tier 2 (5 modules) — 13 modules total — are fully implemented and unit-tested</strong>: config loading, the shared Pydantic schema, seeded RNG management, cost tracking, rate limiting, agent population management, meme pool management, the LiteLLM-backed model gateway, neighbor sampling, stance parsing, vision fallback, logging, and checkpointing.", "<strong>Tier 3 — the integration layer — is designed but not yet written as code.</strong> No <code>simulation_orchestrator.py</code>, no <code>prompt_builder.py</code>, and no CLI/Python API exist in this repository. Every Tier 0/1/2 module's own docstring already describes exactly how it will plug into that not-yet-built orchestrator (referring to \"the frozen-snapshot phase,\" \"the Orchestrator's per-turn sequence,\" etc.), so the intended integration is well-specified even though the integrating code does not exist yet. The single largest concrete gap is <code>prompt_builder.py</code>: no document specifies its prompt template or how persona/language/memory/neighbor content get woven into an actual prompt string — <code>phase3.md</code> names this explicitly as the open question blocking the orchestrator's implementation."]}, {"title": "Major components and communication", "paragraphs": ["See the <strong>Architecture</strong> tab for full per-component detail. At a system level: a <strong>Config Loader</strong> validates a YAML run config into an <code>ExperimentRun</code>. A (planned) <strong>Simulation Orchestrator</strong> would be the only module calling every other component, driving a K-turn loop. Each turn, an <strong>Interaction Engine</strong> selects N neighbors per agent via a tunable alpha-sampling mechanism, and a <strong>Meme Pool Manager</strong> independently decides which scheduled speakers post a meme instead of generating text. Generated-text speakers are dispatched to a <strong>Model Gateway</strong> (itself composed of a <strong>Rate Limiter</strong> and <strong>Cost Tracker</strong>) which normalizes calls to whichever external LLM provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, or a local backend) via LiteLLM. Raw model output passes through a <strong>Stance Parser</strong> to become structured data. A <strong>Logging/Persistence Layer</strong> appends every turn's result to disk, and a <strong>Checkpoint Manager</strong> snapshots full agent state after every turn so an interrupted run can resume."]}, {"title": "External dependencies", "paragraphs": ["<code>litellm</code> is the sole integration point with external LLM providers — no provider SDK is called directly. <code>pydantic</code> (v2) defines every structured type in the system. <code>tenacity</code> implements the Model Gateway's retry-with-backoff policy. <code>pyyaml</code> parses run configs and the pricing table. <code>pandas</code> and <code>statsmodels</code> are already pinned in <code>pyproject.toml</code> for the not-yet-built post-hoc analysis modules. There is no database, no web framework, and no human-facing UI anywhere in the design — this is explicitly a non-goal stated in the architecture docs."]}, {"title": "Data stores", "paragraphs": ["Everything is flat files, not a database — a deliberate non-goal in the design ('no relational database as primary store'). Input assets live under <code>data/personas/*.jsonl</code> (plain-text persona lines) and <code>data/memes/*.jsonl</code> (JSON <code>MemeContent</code> records plus a companion <code>images/</code> directory). <code>pricing_table.yaml</code> at the repo root is the hand-maintained cost table. Output, per completed or in-progress run, lives under <code>runs/{run_id}/</code>: <code>run_config.json</code> (one object), <code>interactions.jsonl</code> (append-only, the system's primary, load-bearing data output — every downstream metric is computed from this), <code>agents_final.jsonl</code> (written once at completion), and <code>checkpoints/latest.json</code> (overwritten each turn)."]}, {"title": "Architectural boundaries and invariants", "paragraphs": ["The dependency-tier boundary is the most important structural rule: a module may only import from a strictly lower tier. Within a turn, a \"frozen snapshot\" boundary (referred to throughout the design docs and code as <strong>Fix F</strong>) guarantees neighbor selection and meme-injection resolution both complete in full <em>before</em> any model dispatch begins for that turn — no agent's turn-t output is ever read by another agent's turn-t neighbor or meme resolution. Error handling draws a hard boundary between <em>fatal</em> failures (an unrecognized model id, a missing pricing entry, a corrupted checkpoint — these always propagate and abort the run) and <em>per-agent-recoverable</em> failures (a stance parse failure after retries, or a non-retryable gateway error — these become one <code>failed_logged_null</code> <code>Interaction</code> record and the run continues for every other agent). Reproducibility is a first-class constraint: every stochastic choice in the system (never LLM sampling itself, which providers don't guarantee deterministic) draws from one of three purpose-specific seeded <code>random.Random</code> streams, never the global <code>random</code> module."]}], "plantuml": "@startuml\nskinparam componentStyle rectangle\n\npackage \"Config & Data (Tier 0 inputs)\" {\n  rectangle \"Config Loader\\n(config_loader.py)\" as ConfigLoader\n  rectangle \"Data Model Layer\\n(models.py)\" as Models\n  rectangle \"Seed Manager\\n(seed_manager.py)\" as SeedMgr\n  database \"data/personas/*.jsonl\\ndata/memes/*.jsonl\" as DataFiles\n  database \"pricing_table.yaml\" as Pricing\n}\n\npackage \"Tier 0 infra\" {\n  rectangle \"Rate Limiter\\n(rate_limiter.py)\" as RateLimiter\n  rectangle \"Cost Tracker\\n(cost_tracker.py)\" as CostTracker\n}\n\npackage \"Tier 1 (implemented)\" {\n  rectangle \"Agent Manager\\n(agent_manager.py)\" as AgentMgr\n  rectangle \"Meme Pool Manager\\n(meme_pool_manager.py)\" as MemePool\n  rectangle \"Model Gateway\\n(model_gateway.py)\" as Gateway\n}\n\npackage \"Tier 2 (implemented)\" {\n  rectangle \"Interaction Engine\\n(interaction_engine.py)\" as IntEngine\n  rectangle \"Stance Parser\\n(stance_parser.py)\" as StanceParser\n  rectangle \"Vision Fallback\\n(vision_fallback.py)\" as VisionFallback\n  rectangle \"Logging Writer\\n(logging_writer.py)\" as LogWriter\n  rectangle \"Checkpoint Manager\\n(checkpoint_manager.py)\" as Checkpoint\n}\n\npackage \"Tier 3 -- PLANNED, not implemented\" #line.dashed {\n  rectangle \"Simulation Orchestrator\\n(simulation_orchestrator.py)\" as Orchestrator #line.dashed\n  rectangle \"Prompt Builder\\n(prompt_builder.py)\" as PromptBuilder #line.dashed\n}\n\npackage \"Planned, not implemented\" #line.dashed {\n  rectangle \"Post-hoc Analysis\\n(stance_regression.py, bimodality_analysis.py, ...)\" as PostHoc #line.dashed\n  rectangle \"CLI + Python API\\n(sandbox/api.py)\" as CliApi #line.dashed\n}\n\ncloud \"External LLM Providers\\n(OpenAI / Anthropic / Google / local, via litellm)\" as External\n\ndatabase \"runs/{run_id}/\\nrun_config.json\\ninteractions.jsonl\\nagents_final.jsonl\\ncheckpoints/\" as RunsDir\n\nactor Researcher\n\nResearcher --> CliApi : YAML config path\nCliApi --> ConfigLoader : load_run_config()\nConfigLoader --> Models : produces ExperimentRun\nConfigLoader --> DataFiles : validates referenced pools exist\nCliApi --> Orchestrator : launch_run()\n\nOrchestrator --> AgentMgr : initialize_population() / apply_interaction()\nOrchestrator --> IntEngine : select_neighbors() per agent per turn\nOrchestrator --> MemePool : resolve_injections_for_turn()\nOrchestrator --> PromptBuilder : build_discussion_prompt()\nOrchestrator --> Gateway : generate() for text speakers\nOrchestrator --> StanceParser : parse_stance() / clamp_and_validate_scale()\nOrchestrator --> LogWriter : write_interaction() / write_run_config() / write_agents_final()\nOrchestrator --> Checkpoint : save() every turn / load() on resume\n\nAgentMgr --> SeedMgr : persona_assignment_rng\nIntEngine --> SeedMgr : neighbor_sampling_rng\nMemePool --> SeedMgr : meme_injection_rng\nAgentMgr --> DataFiles : reads persona pool\nMemePool --> DataFiles : reads meme pool\nPromptBuilder --> VisionFallback : meme-in-prompt substitution\n\nGateway --> RateLimiter : acquire()/release()\nGateway --> CostTracker : record()\nCostTracker --> Pricing : rate lookup\nGateway --> External : litellm.acompletion()\n\nLogWriter --> RunsDir : append/write JSON(L)\nCheckpoint --> RunsDir : read/write checkpoints/latest.json\n\nPostHoc --> RunsDir : reads interactions.jsonl (offline, read-only)\nCliApi --> PostHoc : run_coherence_analysis() / run_bimodality_analysis() / ...\n\nModels .up. AgentMgr\nModels .up. MemePool\nModels .up. IntEngine\nModels .up. Gateway\nModels .up. LogWriter\nModels .up. Checkpoint\nModels .up. ConfigLoader\n@enduml"}, "meta": {"projectName": "sandbox — LLM Agent Echo Chamber Simulation", "description": "A Python simulation of populations of LLM-backed agents discussing a topic over multiple turns under a tunable echo-chamber mechanism, built to answer three research questions about Hinglish vs. English polarization dynamics and meme-driven convergence."}};
